WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.243
- Welcome, everyone.

00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:10.370
I'm really glad to see
everybody here in Luce Hall,

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.220
as well as virtually via Zoom

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.760
to our very special talk this afternoon.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.540
So, my name is Steven Wilkinson,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.480
I'm the Nilekani Professor
of Indian South Asian Studies

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.597
here at Yale

00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:23.680
and the Faculty Director
of the MacMillan Center.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.470
So, the MacMillan Center
is Yale's focal point

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:32.470
for the study of cultures,
societies, languages

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.473
around the world.

00:00:33.473 --> 00:00:36.480
We train our students
to understand the world,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.080
to understand the world's languages.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.950
We send them out in the world to learn.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.100
And we also have the opportunity

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.830
to bring distinguished
visitors here to Yale

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.803
so that we may learn from them here.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.010
Now, I'm really delighted today

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.047
to introduce our featured speaker,

00:00:54.047 --> 00:00:59.047
the Mayor of Warsaw, Rafał Trzaskowski

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.550
and our moderator, Professor Marci Shore,

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.100
who's also the director
of graduate studies

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.960
for our very active
European and Russian studies

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.780
NA Program at the
European Studies Council.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:12.070
And Marci organized this event.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:15.930
So, Mayor Trzaskowski's
title for today's talk,

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.593
is War in Ukraine and a
New Trans-Atlantic agenda.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.560
This event is being supported

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.630
by the George Herbert Walker Jr.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.490
lecture fund in international studies

00:01:27.919 --> 00:01:28.752
here at the MacMillan Center.

00:01:28.752 --> 00:01:31.870
So this was fund established
in honor of Burt Walker

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.303
by the Walker family.

00:01:36.213 --> 00:01:41.213
The Walker family has
produced both Bush Presidents

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.540
who were Yale graduates
are a part of that family.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.003
So, I'm about to note that the mayor

00:01:47.003 --> 00:01:49.245
is delivering one of our first
in-person Walker lectures

00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:50.543
since 2019.

00:01:52.269 --> 00:01:56.580
Mayor Trzaskowski has been the
Mayor of Warsaw since 2018.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.830
He's a member of the
European Committee of Regions

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.720
and the board of Eurocities.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.690
In 2020, he was the
civic platforms candidate

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.140
for the presidency of Poland.

00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:08.350
He's a former member of
the European Parliament,

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.680
vice chair of the European people's party.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.310
And in 2014, he served
as the deputy minister

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.650
of foreign affairs of
the Republican Poland.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.580
And in 2013, as a minister
for administration

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:19.840
and digitization

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.240
in the cabinet of the former
prime minister of Poland,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.650
Donald Tusk.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.000
Mayor Trzaskowski was born in Warsaw,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.080
where he studied at graduated
from the University of Warsaw.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.440
In 2004, he obtained his Ph.D.
degree in political science.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.120
He speaks fluent English,
French, Spanish, Russian,

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.290
and Italian.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:42.290
And moderating his talk today,
is professor Marci Shore.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.360
Professor Shore teaches Modern
European Intellectual History

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.640
here at Yale.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.690
Her research focuses on
the intellectual history

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.230
of 20th and 21 century
Central and Eastern Europe.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.810
She has written many things.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:57.690
She's the translator of Michał
Głowiński, The Black Seasons,

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.840
the author of Caviar and Ashes,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.640
Warsaw Generation's Life and
Death in Marxism, 1918-1968.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.650
The Taste of Ashes,

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.530
The Afterlife of Totalitarianism
in Eastern Europe,

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.010
and The Ukrainian Night,

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.860
an intimate history of revolution.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.510
She was also in 2018,

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.560
a recipient at the very
prestigious Guggenheim Fellowships

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.693
for her current book project.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:25.660
So, thank you to Marci for
moderating today's talk.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.350
The format today is gonna be this,

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.056
we're gonna hear from
Mayor Trzaskowski first

00:03:30.056 --> 00:03:31.660
and then professor Shore

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:35.470
and Mayor Trzaskowski will
sit up front for a discussion

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:37.370
and a Q&amp;A session.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.690
That'll give people the opportunity

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.460
to ask them whatever you like.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.000
Thank you both, and thank
you all for joining us

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:44.833
this afternoon.

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.991
(audience clapping)

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.550
- Yes, hello, good afternoon.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.206
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:59.206 --> 00:04:02.543
It is a honor and a privilege
to be here at the Yale

00:04:02.543 --> 00:04:03.850
and have an opportunity to talk to you

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:07.730
about what's happening
right now in my country

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:08.767
and in my region, of course.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:13.160
And to talk about the Trans
Atlantic Relationship.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.700
And of course, what kind of
impact the situation of today

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.794
has on Trans Atlantic relations.

00:04:18.794 --> 00:04:20.110
I mean, first of all,

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:23.600
I have to tell you that as
it was mentioned before,

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:28.600
I started in European Policy
and I was a think tanker

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.970
for quite a long time
and a university lecturer

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:35.160
and I still am at St.
Petersburg University,

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.210
dealing mostly with the European affairs.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.873
And I worked in the European Parliament.

00:04:39.873 --> 00:04:41.137
I was a member of the European Parliament

00:04:41.137 --> 00:04:43.190
and was a minister of
European Integration.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:46.090
And then I moved into national politics.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:49.345
Some people say one of the
biggest mistakes of my life.

00:04:49.345 --> 00:04:50.178
(audience laugh)

00:04:50.178 --> 00:04:52.782
And I was a minister

00:04:52.782 --> 00:04:55.110
and then I was a member
of National Parliament.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.370
And then I moved to local government.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:58.430
This is pretty unusual

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.700
because usually it's the other way round.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.340
You start with local government,
then you do national,

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.320
then maybe European later on.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.590
And of course, everyone was telling me,

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:10.400
listen, I mean, finally
that's a job of your life

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.670
because you can focus on the future.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.760
You can actually start building
and modernizing your city.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.810
And of course, everything
you do will leave an impact

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.750
because that's what
happens when you're a mayor

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:21.750
of a wonderful city.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.550
And Warsaw of course, is a wonderful city.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:28.610
And you will just focus
on modernizing your city.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.922
And on top of that,

00:05:29.922 --> 00:05:34.140
you will not be subjected
to the political bickering

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:37.111
and partisanship because
people will just simply...

00:05:37.111 --> 00:05:40.770
National media will forget
about you for a while.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.740
And only when there's a small crisis,

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.803
maybe they will be reminded of you.

00:05:46.162 --> 00:05:48.610
And I thought yeah,
well, it's worth a try.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:51.600
And of course, I'm born and bred Warsaw,

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.710
so of course, that was quite a challenge.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.823
After I became mayor, boom,

00:05:58.032 --> 00:06:00.570
a sewer pipe burst under the Vista River.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:03.163
And by the way, it burst twice.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:07.950
So of course, I was mostly
focusing my attention to that.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:11.620
And with the crazy governmental place

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.090
and with the propaganda
that they've unleashed,

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.500
it was not easy.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.200
And then when we just
got after the crisis,

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.508
after the first crisis
when he got out of that,

00:06:20.508 --> 00:06:23.230
of course, COVID hit us.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.550
Four waves of it.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.443
And just as we were getting
out of it, a war happened,

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:31.280
which obviously gives
you quite a perspective

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.770
and sometimes I introduce
myself, not as a mayor of Warsaw,

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.320
but as a minister of crisis situations,

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.630
because all the time, you
have to deal with the crisis,

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:45.060
but that's politics for
you, politics of today.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:48.359
But of course, what
happens in Ukraine today

00:06:48.359 --> 00:06:51.110
is incredibly serious.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:55.110
And it has huge implications
for the security of the region,

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.180
but also for the security of the world.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.187
And that's why we need to
seriously talk about that.

00:07:00.187 --> 00:07:03.208
And the thing is that we
were warning our friends

00:07:03.208 --> 00:07:07.170
in Europe and also in America for years.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:11.750
And we were observing
Vladimir Putin's career,

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.030
and for us at least, it was pretty clear

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.970
who are we dealing with.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:19.420
So we were not misled even at
the beginning of the century

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.300
that this guy could be a good Democrat,

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:25.350
because it was just enough
to study his days in KGB.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:27.270
To study his days in Petersburg

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.103
to sort of guess what
kind of people are we...

00:07:29.103 --> 00:07:31.720
What kind of guy we are dealing with.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.355
And we were telling our friends in Europe

00:07:33.355 --> 00:07:35.250
and we were telling
our friends in America,

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:40.010
don't do deals with thugs or that least,

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.890
think about security.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:46.890
Think about making Poland and
making Europe more independent

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.680
from fossil fuels coming from Russia.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:55.680
Think about putting our energy
into any democratic endeavor

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.163
you can,

00:07:58.163 --> 00:08:01.400
which is going to strengthen our neighbors

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:02.870
to the East of Poland,

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.480
to the so-called post service sphere.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.980
Because our Ukrainian friends
are more than friends,

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:09.670
at the beginning, even our
fellow Russian friends,

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.173
were striving towards democracy.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.470
And of course, everyone was in the U.S.,

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.670
but sometimes even in Europe,

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.930
everyone was sort of lumping
us together as Eastern European

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.230
and thinking that we are no different.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.670
Well, we are, because of course,

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:27.086
we have quite different
democratic experiences,

00:08:27.086 --> 00:08:29.240
but we all wanted the same thing.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:33.930
We wanted to be peaceful,
stable, democratic nations.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.250
And by the way, Ukraine was promised that

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:40.200
when it decided to give
its nuclear weapons away.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.480
It was guaranteed by the Western powers

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:47.100
that the integrity and
sovereignty of Ukraine

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.920
will be protected.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.210
And later on, we were trying all the time

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:53.090
to convince our friends
in Europe and in the U.S.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.610
that we should at least buy that security,

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.170
build an energy union.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.820
I will explain in a second what it is.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:05.510
Build a strong eastern
policy of the European Union.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.660
I remember I started working
in the European Parliament

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:10.310
in 2004, just when Orange Revolution hit

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:12.097
and everyone was hyped up for a while.

00:09:12.097 --> 00:09:14.910
And then we said, "Okay,
now is the to build

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:15.847
the energy union."

00:09:17.741 --> 00:09:19.347
And in a few months, I
mean, the attention went

00:09:19.347 --> 00:09:21.570
and people started thinking
about something different.

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:24.840
And again, we've heard the same spiel.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:26.610
Come on Europe, you're
obsessed with Russia.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.300
I mean, there's such reliable partners,

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.610
even in the Soviet times,
when it came to gas,

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.380
when it came to oil, we could rely on them

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.314
and we could do business with them.

00:09:35.314 --> 00:09:37.360
And now with new Russia, why not?

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.750
And many people were saying,

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.760
if you are investing in
the future of Ukraine,

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.310
investing in the future of Moldova,

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:46.040
trying to promise them,
European Union membership,

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.066
not mentioning any security guarantees,

00:09:48.066 --> 00:09:52.730
then you are actually undermining
the security of Europe.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.790
And you were saying, you
are dealing with thugs.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:56.840
You are dealing with
guys who just understand

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:57.770
the language of power.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.610
And all the time we've
heard, you are obsessed.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:02.430
You don't understand the modernity

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.929
because you're just
there in Eastern Europe

00:10:04.929 --> 00:10:07.610
not seeing the bigger picture.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.450
But fortunately, we were
able to prepare ourselves

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:13.560
at least a bit for what was to come.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:17.730
Look at energy union, it
was an idea of Donald Tusk,

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.484
our former prime minister.

00:10:19.484 --> 00:10:22.240
It was supported of
course, by our politician.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:25.180
It was realized by our governments.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.810
Also when I was minister
of European affairs.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.900
And before we were doing quite a lot

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.190
in the European Parliament.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.100
And what we did, for example,

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:36.160
we made steps to make sure that

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:38.000
we would building energy terminals

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.760
so that we could import gas.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:43.120
What we did, we did inverse flow.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.518
Okay, and the so-called inter connectors,

00:10:45.518 --> 00:10:47.440
which means that just what
10 years ago, 15 years ago,

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:50.340
gas and oil could just flow
one way from Russia to Europe.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.370
Now, we can do the reverse.

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:57.099
We started building inter
connectors with the Baltic States,

00:10:57.099 --> 00:11:00.160
with Slovakia, the Czech
Republic, so on and so forth,

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:04.920
so that we could transport
oil and gas throughout Europe.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:08.920
We also invested in big
reserve wars of gas.

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:12.640
And now it's an obligation
to have those reserve wars

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.560
for at least three months.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.650
And we've also strengthened
the competition policy

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.670
of the European Union so that
you can go after gas problem

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.790
when it is breaking the
rules of competition.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:25.530
We've decoupled two very important things.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:28.420
One is extraction of oil and
then the distribution of oil

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.253
and gas, right?

00:11:29.253 --> 00:11:31.960
So at least because of our insistence,

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:35.330
we are better prepared
to what's happening.

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:38.750
I mean, as you know just
yesterday Russia cut gas

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:43.336
to Poland and to Bulgaria.

00:11:43.336 --> 00:11:45.140
And similarly and simultaneously,

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.610
we were strengthening
the Eastern dimension

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:47.443
of the European Union.

00:11:47.443 --> 00:11:52.420
Investing a lot in those links
with our friends to the east.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.700
And it was tough, boy, it was tough.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:59.670
And I remember talking to
our friends, negotiating it,

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:03.080
and of course, so many hurdles on the way.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:06.210
And if you mentioned north stream,

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:09.254
one north seemed to the pipeline gas pipe

00:12:09.254 --> 00:12:11.260
under the Baltic Sea.

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:12.810
We were warning our friends,

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.350
listen, don't get too
much dependent on Russia.

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:19.340
And again, our arguments were not heard

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:20.737
by our German friends

00:12:20.737 --> 00:12:23.130
and they were telling us
it's a business enterprise.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.630
You shouldn't be so insistent.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:26.463
And then what?

00:12:26.463 --> 00:12:29.840
And then of course,
history proved us right.

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:33.217
And of course, this is a
very bitter pill to swallow.

00:12:33.217 --> 00:12:37.860
And now we have a crisis on our hands

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.803
and a crisis of global dimensions.

00:12:40.729 --> 00:12:44.210
What happens is that of
course, Putin has miscalculated

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:45.350
because he thought first of all,

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:49.090
that he would be able to
divide the Ukrainian society.

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.780
He thought that the Ukrainian
society will be divided,

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.780
that many troops will desert.

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:56.300
That his army will be able
to actually take over Kyiv

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:57.380
in a few days.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.400
He thought that he's going to divide us

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.460
because he was remembering 2014

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.160
when we've agreed on sanctions,

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.690
but they were not very serious.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.340
And again, I was negotiating them.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.640
And when we were telling our friends,

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.900
we thought these sanctions
need to be serious.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.500
We need to go after the oligarchs.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.950
We need to do something about gas and oil.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:16.890
Again, they were saying,
no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:17.930
Step by step.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:22.265
And of course, Putin thought
that with such a weak response

00:13:22.265 --> 00:13:24.680
to Russian aggression in 2014,

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.600
he thought that he could do it again.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.111
And that's what his
intelligence was telling him.

00:13:30.111 --> 00:13:33.050
So, the incredible
thing is that of course,

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.510
he miscalculated when it comes to Ukraine,

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:39.080
because it turned out that
we have a united response.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.880
And by the way, I was
just four or five days

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.740
before the war I was in Kyiv.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.110
And even there people were telling me,

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:47.837
well, yeah, maybe 20%, 30% of
Ukrainian troops will dessert,

00:13:47.837 --> 00:13:51.150
or maybe they will not listen to orders.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.900
There will be two or three
important regional leaders

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:54.970
who might desert.

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:56.696
Nothing of this sort happened.

00:13:56.696 --> 00:13:59.980
And the Ukrainians
really did their lesson.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:04.980
I mean, we've got no time to
go into the military aspects

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:08.070
of it, but really, I mean, after 2014,

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:09.810
they've learned their lesson.

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:12.760
I mean, my favorite thing
is that there is an app.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:16.590
If you are a citizen of
Ukraine, you have that app,

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.603
which is used to communicate
with the government.

00:14:18.603 --> 00:14:20.300
And now it was turned into an app

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:22.927
on which you can inform about
Russian troop movements.

00:14:22.927 --> 00:14:26.890
Make pictures, maps, and
so on and send it directly

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.610
to the authorities and no one can fake it

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:30.700
because if you don't
have a Ukraine identity,

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.060
you can't operate that.

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:32.893
And the Russians,

00:14:32.893 --> 00:14:35.410
they were supposed to have
brilliant communication devices

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:36.730
after the Georgian War.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.960
Now of course, they're using cell phones,

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:42.210
because Putin has created the kleptocracy.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:45.030
I mean, these guys were just
stealing from government.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.750
They were not investing
in modern equipment.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:51.468
And they're fantastic
at doing little mischief

00:14:51.468 --> 00:14:55.130
and hybrid warfare and tactical movement.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.450
But it turned out that they're
not that good at strategy.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.950
Thanks God.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:00.150
So that's the lesson we are learning,

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:02.590
and of course, we should be learning more.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:04.990
Now he has also miscalculated
when it comes to us,

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:05.880
but most importantly,

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:10.880
he's miscalculated when it
comes to the civil society

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:13.630
and the power of the social media.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:17.660
Because I mean, this fight
that we are observing is epic,

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:18.493
and it's so clear.

00:15:18.493 --> 00:15:19.920
It's like David and Goliath.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.540
It's a biblical proportions,

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.028
and it's so clear who's a
good guy, who's a bad guy.

00:15:24.028 --> 00:15:26.508
Sometimes comparing it
for my American audience

00:15:26.508 --> 00:15:28.360
to your pop culture.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:32.640
You have like this marvel
comic ultimate evil,

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:35.210
fighting this every American,

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:37.750
every man who suddenly turns into a hero.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:39.080
Okay? It's so clear.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.930
And that's why the response
of the civil society,

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:46.930
the response of all of us
was so clear and so strong.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:51.500
And the pressure exerted on
elected leaders was so strong.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.240
If someone were to tell me two months ago

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:56.070
that so many American companies
would go out of Russia,

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:58.398
so many German, European companies,

00:15:58.398 --> 00:16:00.174
would go out of Russia,

00:16:00.174 --> 00:16:04.360
I wouldn't have believed hadn't I seen it.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.950
But of course, that's also
because of the pressure

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:08.090
of the civil society.

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:10.320
And here, again, Putin has miscalculated

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.932
because he doesn't understand it.

00:16:11.932 --> 00:16:16.932
And again, it brings us to
the same same thesis that,

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.500
this fight is so clear.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.453
In 2014, it wasn't so clear

00:16:21.453 --> 00:16:24.370
or we didn't tell this story well.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.306
The narrative was a bit different.

00:16:26.306 --> 00:16:29.910
And he's miscalculated when
it comes to our response,

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:32.920
because finally the European Union,

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.300
the United States of
America started responding

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.490
in a concerted and in a tough way.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.112
Because these sanctions bite.

00:16:40.112 --> 00:16:42.790
For the first time, we
went after the oligarchs.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:43.623
For the first time,

00:16:43.623 --> 00:16:45.010
we were talking about

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:47.450
getting ourselves seriously independent

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:51.095
when it comes to Russian fossil fuels.

00:16:51.095 --> 00:16:54.070
And we were taking some tough decision.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:54.903
Can we do more?

00:16:54.903 --> 00:16:55.813
Yes, we can.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.520
Those sanctions can be even tougher,

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:03.222
but Swift, oil and gas,

00:17:03.222 --> 00:17:08.222
American and European companies
out to Russia, that's huge.

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:11.210
And of course, you can always think about

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.670
whether the glass half full or half empty,

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:16.887
but I think that it was
pretty surprising for Putin.

00:17:16.887 --> 00:17:19.140
And of course, we need to do more.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.150
And the important thing is
that we have to persevere.

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:22.670
And the important thing is

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:27.460
that we cannot simply think
that it's going to end soon

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.893
and that then we can relent.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:30.690
And of course,

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:35.116
we are facing one of the biggest
refugee crisis in history

00:17:35.116 --> 00:17:36.540
in Europe,

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:40.173
but also in the world
after the Second World War.

00:17:40.173 --> 00:17:44.990
You know that just three months ago,

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:49.010
Poland was 120th when it
came to accepting refugees,

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.620
some people said 105th

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.720
because there are different statistics.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.354
Now we are second, soon to be first.

00:17:55.354 --> 00:17:58.110
That shows you the
magnitude of the problem.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.400
If you remember the Mediterranean crisis,

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:03.520
when Europe was panicking,
Barb Wire and so on,

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:07.030
and people running a mock,
not knowing how to respond.

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:08.826
We had 200,000 people at a peak,

00:18:08.826 --> 00:18:11.659
200,000 people coming to Europe.

00:18:11.659 --> 00:18:15.119
We have 300,000 people
who came to Warsaw alone

00:18:15.119 --> 00:18:18.100
in a matter of a month.

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.507
So, that shows you the
magnitude of the problem.

00:18:19.507 --> 00:18:23.810
And of course, refugees are
vulnerable people by definition,

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.750
but we have the most vulnerable

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:29.293
because these are usually
mostly young women with kids.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:34.120
I have 120,000 kids in Warsaw.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:36.333
I have 280,000 kids in my schools.

00:18:36.333 --> 00:18:39.384
And because we have granted courageously,

00:18:39.384 --> 00:18:43.490
we've granted Ukrainians
citizen like status,

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.090
they have access to free education,

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:48.763
to free healthcare and to
free social protection.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.960
That means that we should
be accepting 120,000 kids

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:53.793
to our schools.

00:18:53.793 --> 00:18:55.640
We have enrolled already 20,000.

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:58.490
And now we come to the most important part

00:18:59.404 --> 00:19:03.680
of my message to you, is that
what we should do with it.

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:04.620
I mean, the most important thing

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.640
is that there's no strategy, guys.

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:08.230
There's no strategy on a Polish level.

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:09.930
There's no strategy on a European level.

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:12.123
There's no strategy on
an international level.

00:19:12.123 --> 00:19:15.140
Most of what you see is improvisation.

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:18.872
Most of what you see is
not miraculous government,

00:19:18.872 --> 00:19:20.420
central government dealing with it.

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:21.900
It's the people.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.980
The people have accepted
Ukraine to their homes.

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:26.030
Most of us in Poland,

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:28.650
you don't see, I mean,
people come from the U.S.,

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:32.400
from Europe, from different
places, special migration.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.480
And they're amazed.

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:36.301
They say, okay, where are the refugees?

00:19:36.301 --> 00:19:40.290
Because there are no refugee
camps, huge refugee camps.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:44.410
There are no pitch dances in parks.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.860
There are no people in the streets

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:47.610
because they're at our homes.

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:50.715
But of course, the
solidarity which is amazing

00:19:50.715 --> 00:19:55.715
cannot be kept without a
strategy for months and years

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:58.300
because people accepted Ukrainians

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:01.980
for two, three, four months,
but not for eight or nine.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:02.870
Of course, some of them,

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.976
most of them stay with their
friends and with their family.

00:20:05.976 --> 00:20:08.204
So they can, because we had
a huge Ukrainian diaspora

00:20:08.204 --> 00:20:09.238
in Poland before that.

00:20:09.238 --> 00:20:10.260
But some of them stay
with complete strangers.

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:11.730
So we need a strategy.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.170
We need a relocation scheme in Europe

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.410
where it will be coordinated
by the European Union

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.700
where different countries made pledges.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:22.070
And then someone needs to coordinate it.

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:24.040
Because a month ago, I was calling...

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:24.873
In the middle of the night

00:20:24.873 --> 00:20:26.670
I was calling different mayors
from Poland and from Europe

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:29.880
and telling them, please
take 300, take 200 guys,

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:32.653
send us a few buses because
we were overwhelmed.

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:36.330
And this government is
not asking for a strategy

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.620
and it is not authorizing
the European Union to work

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:40.453
because of course,

00:20:40.453 --> 00:20:43.050
they want to get all the political credit.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.460
And I keep telling them guys

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:49.000
no government will be able
to deal with such a crisis.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:51.610
And of course, that's why we
need a push from the Americans,

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:55.430
from our European friends
in order to have a strategy,

00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:59.070
because we have lots of UN
agencies working on the ground.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:01.230
We have European agencies
working on the ground,

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.480
but this haphazard, it's piecemeal,

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:05.740
because the government is
just picking this service,

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.800
this help and so on.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.610
We are having our own strategy in Warsaw,

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:10.710
but that's not enough.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:15.460
Because if I have a
strategy about education,

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:16.840
I told the minister of education,

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:19.665
guys, we cannot accept
120,000 kids overnight.

00:21:19.665 --> 00:21:22.740
Most of them should do distance learning

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.140
on a Ukrainian platform.

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:27.100
And that's what the Ukrainian
Education Ministry want,

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:27.990
right?

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:31.220
That makes more sense.
But there's no strategy.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:32.880
So we are doing it ourselves.

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:35.090
In Warsaw, we are enrolling
people to our schools,

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:36.590
but we are also building those places

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:38.170
in which they can learn online.

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:41.113
We are getting equipment
from donors and so on.

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:43.290
But of course,

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:45.680
because Warsaw is also
the only city in Poland

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:46.890
which has preschools for free

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:49.377
because that was of my electoral program,

00:21:49.377 --> 00:21:51.263
that creates a huge pull factor.

00:21:52.275 --> 00:21:54.360
And again, without a strategy,

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:56.190
it's going to be very
difficult to deal with that.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:58.610
So strategy, strategy, strategy,

00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:01.130
both on a national and a European level.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.750
We have done a lot in the European Union

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:05.020
to regulate the status of refugees.

00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:05.853
But these guys,

00:22:05.853 --> 00:22:07.840
according to the European
law are not refugees.

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:11.113
They are displaced people in
need of temporary protection,

00:22:12.654 --> 00:22:13.740
different directives apply.

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:15.380
So, again, I'm gonna give you an example,

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:18.370
if you're a refugee and if
you get registered in Poland,

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:21.810
if you go to Germany, then
you lose any social protection

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:23.810
because the European Union wants to fight

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:27.010
with secondary movements
and with a possibility

00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:30.040
to choose the country of your asylum,

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:32.350
because that would mean that
everyone would go to Germany

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:35.410
or to Sweden because that's
where the conditions are best.

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:38.930
But these guys, again, are not refugees.

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:41.900
So for example, they ask me if I register,

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:43.960
do I lose my social rights,

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:45.920
if then I go to the
Netherlands or to Germany?

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:46.940
And I cannot answer them

00:22:46.940 --> 00:22:49.760
because we don't have a
one system Europe on that.

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.490
So, that's why we need
a European strategy.

00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:55.050
And I could go on and on and
give you some other examples

00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:55.883
of that.

00:22:55.883 --> 00:22:57.455
And of course, when it comes to support,

00:22:57.455 --> 00:22:59.410
we need that support

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:00.800
not only to go to the central government,

00:23:00.800 --> 00:23:01.640
but we need that support

00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:03.680
to go to the non-governmental
organizations.

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:06.420
By the way, exactly the same
non-governmental organizations

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:07.843
that now save our day,

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:11.350
were the ones that were
deprived of financing

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:12.740
by the populist government,

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:14.030
those who help with refugees,

00:23:14.030 --> 00:23:17.074
those who help with women's
rights, children trafficking,

00:23:17.074 --> 00:23:21.170
LGBT community and so on and so forth.

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:23.170
Those are the guys who are now helping us

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.660
and now are saving the day.

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:27.090
So the money should go to refugees,

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:29.855
to non-government
organizations and also to us.

00:23:29.855 --> 00:23:32.230
And that's also the message
that I'm trying to sell

00:23:32.230 --> 00:23:35.170
in Europe and to our American friends.

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:38.180
And now finally, in the last
few minutes about job politics,

00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:40.790
because everyone is
asking the same questions,

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:41.623
what's gonna happen?

00:23:41.623 --> 00:23:43.070
We don't know what's gonna happen.

00:23:43.070 --> 00:23:46.860
And you've heard because I
assume that you are interested

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:48.950
in what's happening if you're here.

00:23:48.950 --> 00:23:52.383
You heard Putin in just
yesterday saying that

00:23:52.383 --> 00:23:57.383
they might escalate that those myths,

00:23:58.210 --> 00:24:00.480
that there is a Polish American plot

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:03.070
to send our soldiers into
Ukraine and so on and so forth.

00:24:03.070 --> 00:24:04.847
This is really worrying.

00:24:04.847 --> 00:24:08.400
And of course, these guys
are threatening to escalate.

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:10.332
They're escalating already in the east.

00:24:10.332 --> 00:24:13.800
They're threatening to
maybe go to another level,

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:18.800
but I tell you one thing, I
mean, the thugs and bullies,

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:22.340
and some of us know it
from our neighborhood

00:24:22.340 --> 00:24:24.335
and from our high school

00:24:24.335 --> 00:24:27.030
understand only the word of strength

00:24:27.030 --> 00:24:29.573
or the reality of strength.

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:32.570
So we need to stay united.

00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:37.570
We need to send clear signals to Russia.

00:24:37.570 --> 00:24:39.420
We shouldn't lose it from sight,

00:24:39.420 --> 00:24:40.253
because again,

00:24:40.253 --> 00:24:42.900
I'm afraid that after two,
three, four, five months,

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:46.220
people will turn their attention
to something different.

00:24:46.220 --> 00:24:49.720
And of course, the end game
is very difficult to foresee

00:24:49.720 --> 00:24:52.430
because maybe Putin is looking
for a face saving exercise.

00:24:52.430 --> 00:24:54.620
We don't know, but what if he finds one

00:24:54.620 --> 00:24:56.900
and then it's unacceptable
to our Ukrainian friends?

00:24:56.900 --> 00:24:58.280
What do we do then?

00:24:58.280 --> 00:25:02.290
And of course, what do
we do with the crisis

00:25:02.290 --> 00:25:05.240
which is at our hands,
the humanitarian crisis,

00:25:05.240 --> 00:25:07.610
because we've opened our
Ukrainian brothers and sisters

00:25:07.610 --> 00:25:09.770
and we will keep on doing so,

00:25:09.770 --> 00:25:12.780
but we probably are going
to have a second wave

00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:14.780
of just three or four days ago.

00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:16.620
No, five days ago, before coming here,

00:25:16.620 --> 00:25:18.954
I talked to people from Donbas
and they were telling me

00:25:18.954 --> 00:25:22.500
we were there for seven, eight years

00:25:22.500 --> 00:25:24.360
in the war zone and we didn't move.

00:25:24.360 --> 00:25:27.210
But after what we've seen in Bucha happen,

00:25:27.210 --> 00:25:30.970
we decided to move, and
they're moving to Poland.

00:25:30.970 --> 00:25:32.500
So, of course, we cannot do it alone

00:25:32.500 --> 00:25:34.733
and we need assistance and we need help.

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:39.793
And of course, that has huge
implications for our security.

00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:43.020
There's always a silver lining

00:25:43.020 --> 00:25:45.272
because the important stuff

00:25:45.272 --> 00:25:50.030
is also that the century
of historical experiences

00:25:50.030 --> 00:25:51.370
can be turned overnight

00:25:52.474 --> 00:25:55.510
and we can build a much
sounder and better foundation

00:25:55.510 --> 00:25:58.400
for our relations with
our Ukrainian friends.

00:25:58.400 --> 00:26:01.940
This is incredibly important
for the stability of the region

00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:06.370
and for the chance of those
posts of states to be integrated

00:26:06.370 --> 00:26:08.343
to the European community.

00:26:09.340 --> 00:26:11.150
But the important thing is,

00:26:11.150 --> 00:26:13.976
also that some of them
will stay in Poland.

00:26:13.976 --> 00:26:16.290
Many of them will go back

00:26:16.290 --> 00:26:18.240
with completely different expectations,

00:26:19.330 --> 00:26:21.550
building a democratic state.

00:26:21.550 --> 00:26:24.080
I meet them on the ground
and at the beginning,

00:26:24.080 --> 00:26:25.810
and I speak Russian.

00:26:25.810 --> 00:26:26.997
So it's a bit more easy.

00:26:26.997 --> 00:26:29.292
And they look at me and
I tell them I'm a mayor.

00:26:29.292 --> 00:26:31.150
I want to help and so on in Russia

00:26:31.150 --> 00:26:32.933
and most of them don't believe me.

00:26:32.933 --> 00:26:35.830
A mayor at a railway station

00:26:35.830 --> 00:26:37.880
with no security guards speaking to me

00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:39.150
and everything's for free?

00:26:39.150 --> 00:26:41.310
We need to ask our Ukraine volunteers

00:26:41.310 --> 00:26:43.321
to explain that this is not a scam,

00:26:43.321 --> 00:26:46.620
that I don't want to cheat
them out of their money.

00:26:46.620 --> 00:26:49.860
But these expectations will
be carried back, we hope.

00:26:49.860 --> 00:26:52.400
And that will allow our Ukrainian friends

00:26:52.400 --> 00:26:55.080
to create a democratic society in Ukraine.

00:26:55.080 --> 00:27:00.060
So, that's the positive angle to it.

00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:05.060
But of course, still this
huge geopolitical problem

00:27:06.430 --> 00:27:08.050
is ahead of us.

00:27:08.050 --> 00:27:11.990
And we need to get our heads
together and try to resolve it.

00:27:11.990 --> 00:27:13.340
And it's not gonna be easy.

00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:16.600
So, I'll stop here, guys,

00:27:16.600 --> 00:27:20.070
because I know that you
want to probably ask

00:27:20.070 --> 00:27:23.720
quite a few questions and Marci as well,

00:27:23.720 --> 00:27:27.323
so that we can move
fluidly to the second part.

00:27:28.880 --> 00:27:30.380
And I always finish all my lectures,

00:27:30.380 --> 00:27:35.380
all my talks the same way
today in this day and age.

00:27:35.618 --> 00:27:37.346
(speaking in foreign language)

00:27:37.346 --> 00:27:40.700
(audience speaking in foreign language)

00:27:40.700 --> 00:27:44.159
- I have the feeling of a tear in time

00:27:44.159 --> 00:27:46.780
that you have a dramatic
historical moment,

00:27:46.780 --> 00:27:48.576
the sense that one world has ended,

00:27:48.576 --> 00:27:50.750
and whatever happens next,

00:27:50.750 --> 00:27:52.763
we're going to be in another world.

00:27:54.420 --> 00:27:57.350
A couple days before the invasion started,

00:27:57.350 --> 00:27:59.950
our friend Svyatoslav Vakarchuk.

00:27:59.950 --> 00:28:02.330
I'm sure you know that Ukrainian rockstar

00:28:02.330 --> 00:28:03.880
who spent the semester here at Yale.

00:28:03.880 --> 00:28:05.456
So, many of you know him.

00:28:05.456 --> 00:28:07.067
I called, and I said,

00:28:07.067 --> 00:28:10.500
"Svyatoslav, what is the
atmosphere like in Kyiv?"

00:28:10.500 --> 00:28:11.939
And he said, "Well, Marci,

00:28:11.939 --> 00:28:16.939
imagine a synthesis between
Florida in October 1961

00:28:18.620 --> 00:28:20.465
during the Cuban Missile Crisis

00:28:20.465 --> 00:28:25.465
and Central Europe between
the Munich Agreement of 1938,

00:28:26.030 --> 00:28:28.300
the invasion of Poland in 1939.

00:28:28.300 --> 00:28:30.147
It's something like that."

00:28:32.920 --> 00:28:35.640
And there was a sense that
nobody knew what was coming,

00:28:35.640 --> 00:28:38.640
but one of the things
that I think Ukrainians

00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:41.660
and Poles share is an understanding

00:28:41.660 --> 00:28:43.490
that everything is possible.

00:28:43.490 --> 00:28:44.740
Americans don't have this.

00:28:44.740 --> 00:28:47.770
Americans think their
constraints on reality.

00:28:47.770 --> 00:28:48.920
After Trump was elected,

00:28:48.920 --> 00:28:51.800
people were walking around
saying, okay, this is bad.

00:28:51.800 --> 00:28:53.990
This is very bad, but
we're gonna get through it.

00:28:53.990 --> 00:28:55.280
We have checks and balances,

00:28:55.280 --> 00:28:57.498
checks and balances was
repeated like a yoga mantra.

00:28:57.498 --> 00:28:59.670
Whereas east Europeans,

00:28:59.670 --> 00:29:01.730
I feel like know that
everything can look normal,

00:29:01.730 --> 00:29:03.500
but it can turn on a dime

00:29:03.500 --> 00:29:05.140
and you have to somehow
be prepared for that,

00:29:05.140 --> 00:29:07.490
even if it's in pot
possible to be prepared.

00:29:07.490 --> 00:29:11.242
So my first question is that
given that tear and time,

00:29:11.242 --> 00:29:14.270
what has surprised you most

00:29:14.270 --> 00:29:16.510
that you would not have
been able to conceive

00:29:16.510 --> 00:29:17.563
of three months ago?

00:29:19.020 --> 00:29:20.100
- Well, quite a few things.

00:29:20.100 --> 00:29:22.560
I mean, I've just tried to
talk about it for half an hour,

00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:25.750
how surprising it was for many
of us at the end of the day,

00:29:25.750 --> 00:29:29.944
because we all knew
that something is brewed

00:29:29.944 --> 00:29:32.237
and we were also informed about it.

00:29:32.237 --> 00:29:35.628
And we took it seriously,
but everyone I talked to,

00:29:35.628 --> 00:29:38.020
five days before the war in Kyiv

00:29:38.020 --> 00:29:40.870
was telling me it's gonna be
another hybrid war for a bit

00:29:42.924 --> 00:29:45.740
but no one expected a
full out war seriously.

00:29:45.740 --> 00:29:47.910
I mean, so that of course, was surprising,

00:29:47.910 --> 00:29:51.910
but what really surprised me
is this incredible resilience

00:29:51.910 --> 00:29:53.110
of the Ukrainian people.

00:29:55.510 --> 00:29:57.930
And when they come to
Warsaw, they're so proud.

00:29:57.930 --> 00:29:59.957
Most of them just wanna work and they say,

00:29:59.957 --> 00:30:02.240
"We do want to rely on anyone.

00:30:02.240 --> 00:30:04.550
We just want to earn our upkeep."

00:30:04.550 --> 00:30:09.110
And this is incredibly
heartening and amazing.

00:30:09.110 --> 00:30:11.495
But also the response,

00:30:11.495 --> 00:30:16.495
the concerted and unequivocal
response of the west,

00:30:17.650 --> 00:30:20.240
because of this pressure
of the social media,

00:30:20.240 --> 00:30:22.667
I mean, if someone were to
tell me, I told you about it,

00:30:22.667 --> 00:30:23.910
just two months ago

00:30:23.910 --> 00:30:28.686
that this pressure would
be so, so, so important,

00:30:28.686 --> 00:30:31.500
I wouldn't believe.

00:30:31.500 --> 00:30:32.500
And now the question of course,

00:30:32.500 --> 00:30:35.510
is whether that is going to be continued.

00:30:35.510 --> 00:30:36.710
And that's a big question.

00:30:36.710 --> 00:30:38.519
So there are quite a lot of surprises.

00:30:38.519 --> 00:30:41.926
The Polish people didn't surprise me

00:30:41.926 --> 00:30:45.260
because after years of
this populous government

00:30:45.260 --> 00:30:46.960
who was trying to fight with

00:30:46.960 --> 00:30:49.070
and threaten everyone with refugees

00:30:49.070 --> 00:30:51.890
and threaten everyone
with the LGBT community

00:30:51.890 --> 00:30:54.010
and threaten everyone with
all kinds of minorities,

00:30:54.010 --> 00:30:55.970
because they always need an enemy,

00:30:55.970 --> 00:30:58.680
I knew that there is this
instinct of solidarity

00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:00.630
that we have in our DNA.

00:31:00.630 --> 00:31:01.463
By the way,

00:31:01.463 --> 00:31:03.423
I negotiated that as a
minister of European affairs,

00:31:03.423 --> 00:31:05.810
that we would accept 7,000 refugees

00:31:05.810 --> 00:31:07.470
in the Mediterranean crisis.

00:31:07.470 --> 00:31:10.010
And the populist government was telling us

00:31:10.010 --> 00:31:14.762
that they're going to change
the way we live 7,000.

00:31:14.762 --> 00:31:15.816
And at a moment,

00:31:15.816 --> 00:31:19.909
7,000 were crossing our
border in 10 minutes.

00:31:19.909 --> 00:31:24.037
So that also shows you
the level of manipulation.

00:31:24.037 --> 00:31:26.863
It's quite a lot of surprises.

00:31:29.846 --> 00:31:30.679
- Okay.

00:31:30.679 --> 00:31:33.340
So, I'll ask one more quite
self-interested question,

00:31:33.340 --> 00:31:37.076
just that, some of us here
like myself among them,

00:31:37.076 --> 00:31:40.150
have been in the role of
the cultural mediators

00:31:40.150 --> 00:31:43.380
and the translators, trying
to explain eastern Europe

00:31:43.380 --> 00:31:44.740
to Americans.

00:31:44.740 --> 00:31:47.340
And if this were an ordinary situation,

00:31:47.340 --> 00:31:49.240
I would feel like this is
going extraordinarily well,

00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:50.670
we've never gotten so much attention.

00:31:50.670 --> 00:31:53.210
The journalists are asking
better and better questions here.

00:31:53.210 --> 00:31:56.050
We're better able to connect
our Ukrainian colleagues

00:31:56.050 --> 00:31:57.260
with American editors.

00:31:57.260 --> 00:32:01.894
And I'm still asking myself,
like what could we do better?

00:32:01.894 --> 00:32:06.010
Do you have impression that
there are things here in America

00:32:06.010 --> 00:32:09.870
that Americans by and large
don't yet understand well enough

00:32:09.870 --> 00:32:13.155
that are crucial, that we
should be on point about?

00:32:13.155 --> 00:32:17.260
- Well, again, I mean,
of course, but listen,

00:32:17.260 --> 00:32:21.474
I mean, President Biden was in Warsaw

00:32:21.474 --> 00:32:25.410
where I had a chance and honor to show him

00:32:25.410 --> 00:32:28.723
the place where we register Ukrainians.

00:32:30.022 --> 00:32:34.680
And the strongest words possible
about defending every inch

00:32:34.680 --> 00:32:35.810
of NATO territory.

00:32:35.810 --> 00:32:38.040
I went to the east on numerous occasions

00:32:38.040 --> 00:32:40.260
and the Patriot missiles.

00:32:40.260 --> 00:32:43.270
I mean, everywhere,
they're American soldiers,

00:32:43.270 --> 00:32:46.270
the 82nd, but only everywhere.

00:32:46.270 --> 00:32:48.930
I mean, the reality changed so much.

00:32:48.930 --> 00:32:51.540
And the response of the Western,

00:32:51.540 --> 00:32:52.660
the response and the interest

00:32:52.660 --> 00:32:55.010
of the American society's unbelievable.

00:32:55.010 --> 00:33:00.010
I mean, listen all my friends
keep asking me, calling me.

00:33:00.250 --> 00:33:04.550
I see Ukrainian flags on all social media.

00:33:04.550 --> 00:33:06.680
I see in New York, all the Russians,

00:33:06.680 --> 00:33:09.690
some of our in vodka places
turning into Ukrainian.

00:33:09.690 --> 00:33:11.925
Some of our, in vodka places.

00:33:11.925 --> 00:33:16.925
The behavior of celebrities
and so on and so forth.

00:33:18.870 --> 00:33:21.989
This is unheard of and
the level of interest.

00:33:21.989 --> 00:33:24.977
So, I'm not sure that we can do more.

00:33:24.977 --> 00:33:29.977
The important thing that we
draw a lesson from it, okay?

00:33:30.130 --> 00:33:32.200
And that we translate it into action.

00:33:32.200 --> 00:33:36.480
And that we explain that
this is huge ramifications

00:33:36.480 --> 00:33:37.890
for our security.

00:33:37.890 --> 00:33:40.360
And by the way, not only
for Russian, Ukraine,

00:33:40.360 --> 00:33:42.030
because all the thugs in the world,

00:33:42.030 --> 00:33:44.308
all the dictators are looking at it,

00:33:44.308 --> 00:33:46.280
and they're thinking, okay.

00:33:46.280 --> 00:33:49.660
I mean, the west sometimes
can pull it together

00:33:49.660 --> 00:33:50.810
and they can be tough.

00:33:50.810 --> 00:33:52.857
They can respond in a uniform fashion.

00:33:52.857 --> 00:33:56.740
Okay, maybe being aggressive costs a lot.

00:33:56.740 --> 00:33:58.320
Maybe we should rethink it.

00:33:58.320 --> 00:34:01.750
I mean, that's also the reality of today.

00:34:01.750 --> 00:34:03.060
Let's hope.

00:34:03.060 --> 00:34:08.060
So I guess, I've seen all
the American journalists

00:34:08.890 --> 00:34:13.235
in Warsaw and really well informed.

00:34:13.235 --> 00:34:16.890
I never had so much air
time on American television

00:34:16.890 --> 00:34:19.810
in my life, of course.

00:34:19.810 --> 00:34:21.270
And it's not only about me,

00:34:21.270 --> 00:34:23.920
of course, politicians
always talk about themselves.

00:34:23.920 --> 00:34:26.423
Fortunately in America,
you're allowed to do that.

00:34:27.320 --> 00:34:32.320
But there is this window
of opportunity to inform,

00:34:32.980 --> 00:34:35.480
but also to draw conclusions from, okay?

00:34:35.480 --> 00:34:37.610
And to explain what's what

00:34:37.610 --> 00:34:39.560
and to explain that we need to be united,

00:34:39.560 --> 00:34:42.290
that we need to draw inclusion from it,

00:34:42.290 --> 00:34:45.930
to offer Ukraine a European
perspective seriously.

00:34:45.930 --> 00:34:47.860
Which would've never happened,

00:34:47.860 --> 00:34:50.710
to make ourselves
independent of fossil fuels

00:34:50.710 --> 00:34:52.100
coming from Russia.

00:34:52.100 --> 00:34:53.440
Today, I was just elected

00:34:53.440 --> 00:34:58.042
for the board of the Convent of Mayors

00:34:58.042 --> 00:35:01.010
where we fight with climate change.

00:35:01.010 --> 00:35:03.990
And I say, this is the
moment where we should seek

00:35:03.990 --> 00:35:06.380
for synergies to save our planet,

00:35:06.380 --> 00:35:07.530
to fight with climate change,

00:35:07.530 --> 00:35:10.530
to make ourselves
independent of fossil fuels

00:35:10.530 --> 00:35:12.780
in general and fossil
fuels coming from Russia.

00:35:12.780 --> 00:35:16.237
Okay, we need a transition
period, of course.

00:35:16.237 --> 00:35:19.110
But because it's not
gonna happen overnight,

00:35:19.110 --> 00:35:20.040
but that's should,

00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:22.360
I mean, the pandemic
and the crisis in Russia

00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:25.901
should push us all of the decision makers

00:35:25.901 --> 00:35:29.010
into making the right decisions.

00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:29.843
And on top of that,

00:35:29.843 --> 00:35:32.603
that also allows us to see who's who.

00:35:34.880 --> 00:35:38.840
Remember Trump and how he go sit up

00:35:38.840 --> 00:35:40.960
to some Russian politicians.

00:35:40.960 --> 00:35:45.700
Remember Salvie Lapan, the
populist government in Poland,

00:35:45.700 --> 00:35:48.920
also liking those populists
who were financed by Russia.

00:35:48.920 --> 00:35:50.735
I mean, let's not conclusions from it.

00:35:50.735 --> 00:35:53.952
Some of them did suddenly like...

00:35:53.952 --> 00:35:57.860
Half a year ago, we were
telling the populist in Poland,

00:35:57.860 --> 00:36:00.840
why have you removed
all the European flags

00:36:00.840 --> 00:36:01.810
from your ministries?

00:36:01.810 --> 00:36:03.600
And they're only Polish ones.

00:36:03.600 --> 00:36:05.400
By the way, the Polish
flag is the most beautiful

00:36:05.400 --> 00:36:06.611
in the world.

00:36:06.611 --> 00:36:07.444
(Marci laughs)

00:36:07.444 --> 00:36:10.030
But why have you removed
the European ones?

00:36:10.030 --> 00:36:11.640
They're back.

00:36:11.640 --> 00:36:13.350
All of the European flags are there,

00:36:13.350 --> 00:36:14.930
and all the NATO flags are there.

00:36:14.930 --> 00:36:16.900
Good. They're learning a lesson.

00:36:16.900 --> 00:36:19.100
I mean, so we should
also learn the lesson.

00:36:19.100 --> 00:36:21.360
And this is the thing we should be doing,

00:36:21.360 --> 00:36:22.650
explaining to the American people,

00:36:22.650 --> 00:36:24.870
explaining to the Europeans guys, come on.

00:36:24.870 --> 00:36:26.480
Hello, crisis.

00:36:26.480 --> 00:36:29.970
Imagine if Trump was president
of the United States now,

00:36:29.970 --> 00:36:32.212
Jesus Christ almighty.

00:36:32.212 --> 00:36:33.100
(Marci laughs)

00:36:33.100 --> 00:36:35.135
People are telling me,
people are asking me,

00:36:35.135 --> 00:36:36.950
aren't you afraid?

00:36:36.950 --> 00:36:39.480
And I'm saying, if President
Zelensky is not panicking,

00:36:39.480 --> 00:36:41.490
I'm not panicking either.

00:36:41.490 --> 00:36:44.410
But thanks God we have
the leaders we have.

00:36:44.410 --> 00:36:46.513
Imagine Lappen won France.

00:36:49.627 --> 00:36:52.432
I mean, we should be drawing conclusions.

00:36:52.432 --> 00:36:56.513
The electoral process is not a game,

00:36:57.670 --> 00:37:00.640
many people dislike
mainstream political parties.

00:37:00.640 --> 00:37:01.833
I understand that.

00:37:02.843 --> 00:37:04.460
But at the end of the day,

00:37:04.460 --> 00:37:09.173
unfortunately, most of the
time we vote for lesser evil.

00:37:10.470 --> 00:37:13.520
Most of the time we need
to vote with our brain

00:37:13.520 --> 00:37:15.733
at the end of the day,
not only with our heart.

00:37:17.170 --> 00:37:20.853
So this is the point we
should be driving home.

00:37:22.070 --> 00:37:24.850
And believe you me, people
understand it in U.S.

00:37:24.850 --> 00:37:25.683
Five years ago

00:37:25.683 --> 00:37:27.568
when I was talking about
problems with democracy,

00:37:27.568 --> 00:37:30.620
I was seeing it in my friend's eyes.

00:37:30.620 --> 00:37:33.140
Yeah, this guy from the barren east,

00:37:33.140 --> 00:37:35.270
what does he know about democracy?

00:37:35.270 --> 00:37:36.150
Trump was elected

00:37:36.150 --> 00:37:38.910
and suddenly my American friends
started understanding me,

00:37:38.910 --> 00:37:40.010
attack on the Capital,

00:37:40.010 --> 00:37:41.410
and everyone understands me.

00:37:42.820 --> 00:37:44.013
And by the way,

00:37:44.920 --> 00:37:48.960
Poland should be the strongest
democracy in Europe now.

00:37:48.960 --> 00:37:52.310
We cannot afford a weakest
link on our eastern border.

00:37:52.310 --> 00:37:55.360
