not just the Polish one,
looking to score points on this,

00:50:30.523 --> 00:50:34.730
a lot of the points that have been used

00:50:34.730 --> 00:50:37.400
as criticisms for peace, right?

00:50:37.400 --> 00:50:41.515
That the LGBTQ rights, women's rights,

00:50:41.515 --> 00:50:43.805
judicial reform, etc,

00:50:43.805 --> 00:50:46.900
those topics have kind of be compared,

00:50:46.900 --> 00:50:50.610
and I think that's probably
integrated in Yale.

00:50:50.610 --> 00:50:51.870
They're very happy about that.

00:50:51.870 --> 00:50:56.670
So, how do you or what is your plans,

00:50:56.670 --> 00:50:58.777
you are a member of your opposition party

00:50:58.777 --> 00:51:02.200
to see that those points remain salient

00:51:02.200 --> 00:51:04.010
and make sure that Europe is prepared

00:51:04.010 --> 00:51:08.030
and is welcoming to be people who happen

00:51:08.030 --> 00:51:09.570
to not be Europeans next time?

00:51:09.570 --> 00:51:10.630
- Got you.

00:51:10.630 --> 00:51:11.463
Okay.

00:51:11.463 --> 00:51:12.364
So first of all,

00:51:12.364 --> 00:51:15.547
when it comes to the European
perspective for Ukraine,

00:51:15.547 --> 00:51:17.330
I mean, that's a very good question

00:51:17.330 --> 00:51:21.010
because I think that things have changed

00:51:21.010 --> 00:51:25.700
in the heads of a lot
of European politicians.

00:51:25.700 --> 00:51:28.280
So for the first time,
because they were telling us

00:51:28.280 --> 00:51:29.560
it's impossible.

00:51:29.560 --> 00:51:32.550
Ukraine Moldova, not now.

00:51:32.550 --> 00:51:35.350
And you've seen the
progress of the negotiations

00:51:35.350 --> 00:51:37.520
with the Balkans States
and so on and so forth.

00:51:37.520 --> 00:51:38.530
So now it's the moment,

00:51:38.530 --> 00:51:40.790
that's the window of
opportunity to speed it up.

00:51:40.790 --> 00:51:43.500
Of course, it took us more than a decade

00:51:43.500 --> 00:51:44.750
from the first declaration

00:51:44.750 --> 00:51:46.620
to actually enter the European Union

00:51:46.620 --> 00:51:48.580
from the association agreement

00:51:48.580 --> 00:51:53.500
to the membership more than 13 years.

00:51:53.500 --> 00:51:56.900
But of course, now is the
moment to drive that point home

00:51:56.900 --> 00:52:00.570
and to start the process.

00:52:00.570 --> 00:52:03.380
But again, you know for how long

00:52:03.380 --> 00:52:05.500
Turkey has been negotiating membership

00:52:05.500 --> 00:52:06.333
with the European Union?

00:52:06.333 --> 00:52:08.670
From at least 1968.

00:52:08.670 --> 00:52:11.360
So, but now's the moment
and that's my answer.

00:52:11.360 --> 00:52:13.250
And now we should be driving it

00:52:13.250 --> 00:52:16.821
and keeping it on the agenda
of the European Union.

00:52:16.821 --> 00:52:19.290
Because that's the only way forward.

00:52:19.290 --> 00:52:20.990
And by the way, the
Russians even said NATO,

00:52:20.990 --> 00:52:22.760
no European Union, okay.

00:52:22.760 --> 00:52:25.510
By the way, you know the
membership in the European Union

00:52:25.510 --> 00:52:29.860
would be not much more.

00:52:29.860 --> 00:52:33.710
But as serious a guarantee
to the Ukrainians

00:52:33.710 --> 00:52:38.710
that they will remain a part
of the west as anything else.

00:52:38.770 --> 00:52:41.250
When it comes to what
you said about refugees.

00:52:41.250 --> 00:52:44.040
I don't think that
Europe will ever be ready

00:52:44.040 --> 00:52:45.760
in a sense that welcoming and so on.

00:52:45.760 --> 00:52:48.230
This is the hardest topic ever.

00:52:48.230 --> 00:52:51.270
The hot button is you
look at the United States

00:52:51.270 --> 00:52:52.430
and so on and forth.

00:52:52.430 --> 00:52:54.500
We are better prepared than we used to be.

00:52:54.500 --> 00:52:57.580
Because finally, we have
a lot of instruments.

00:52:57.580 --> 00:53:01.370
We have the instruments for
helping in the third countries.

00:53:01.370 --> 00:53:02.570
We have instruments

00:53:02.570 --> 00:53:06.700
when it comes to relocating
immigrants within,

00:53:06.700 --> 00:53:08.427
dealing with secondary movements,

00:53:08.427 --> 00:53:10.902
we have European border guards.

00:53:10.902 --> 00:53:13.750
We've done quite a lot of things

00:53:13.750 --> 00:53:15.930
in order to prepare ourselves, okay?

00:53:15.930 --> 00:53:17.900
For different type of crises.

00:53:17.900 --> 00:53:21.844
We have all of those
readmission agreements.

00:53:21.844 --> 00:53:25.800
Finally, we have one
migration policy in Europe

00:53:25.800 --> 00:53:28.320
because it used to be
completely fragmented,

00:53:28.320 --> 00:53:29.720
but are we prepared?

00:53:29.720 --> 00:53:31.550
If we're gonna have millions and millions

00:53:31.550 --> 00:53:32.610
of additional refugees,

00:53:32.610 --> 00:53:35.810
of course, it always is going
to be a political problem.

00:53:35.810 --> 00:53:38.380
And it is politically incorrect to say,

00:53:38.380 --> 00:53:41.640
but in a Polish case,
these guys look like us.

00:53:41.640 --> 00:53:43.760
They speak a very similar language,

00:53:43.760 --> 00:53:45.160
there's this cultural affinity

00:53:45.160 --> 00:53:46.290
and they fight for our freedom.

00:53:46.290 --> 00:53:48.840
So of course, it is easier to accept that

00:53:48.840 --> 00:53:50.400
than to accept someone else.

00:53:50.400 --> 00:53:53.608
And of course, it is very
difficult to wage a populist

00:53:53.608 --> 00:53:57.460
fight against it because
no one would believe in it.

00:53:57.460 --> 00:53:59.270
And even the populist realized that.

00:53:59.270 --> 00:54:03.012
So I mean, unfortunately,

00:54:03.012 --> 00:54:06.260
I don't think that we will
ever be politically prepared

00:54:06.260 --> 00:54:07.093
for that,

00:54:07.093 --> 00:54:09.740
but of course, a lot is
changing in people's mentality

00:54:09.740 --> 00:54:12.783
because they see that 7,000,
it's not a problem, right?

00:54:13.794 --> 00:54:18.794
And of course, the non-Ukrainians,
I said that in my speech,

00:54:19.430 --> 00:54:22.840
this is a hot issue for the government,

00:54:22.840 --> 00:54:24.060
what to do with them.

00:54:24.060 --> 00:54:26.110
And of course, there are
questions of integration.

00:54:26.110 --> 00:54:29.560
I mean, now everyone is
saying, Poland did a great job,

00:54:29.560 --> 00:54:31.330
but in a month or two or three or four,

00:54:31.330 --> 00:54:35.150
if no one help us out,
we will have a backlash.

00:54:35.150 --> 00:54:37.140
And then there are questions
that if there is no strategy,

00:54:37.140 --> 00:54:39.363
what should I do with 120,000 kids?

00:54:39.363 --> 00:54:42.883
I cannot accept them all
to our schools, right?

00:54:42.883 --> 00:54:44.897
And then there is a
question of integration,

00:54:44.897 --> 00:54:48.180
and then there is a question,
how do we envisage the future?

00:54:48.180 --> 00:54:49.743
It's hellishly complicated.

00:54:49.743 --> 00:54:52.070
And by the way, if we don't do anything

00:54:52.070 --> 00:54:53.310
about climate change,

00:54:53.310 --> 00:54:55.074
we're going to have hundreds of,

00:54:55.074 --> 00:54:58.310
millions of people on the move.

00:54:58.310 --> 00:55:01.900
So that's again, this is a
moment to drive that point home.

00:55:01.900 --> 00:55:03.743
Now, about Polish situation.

00:55:04.670 --> 00:55:08.310
Well, I could tell you draw
one very important conclusion.

00:55:08.310 --> 00:55:10.494
And here I differ from
some of my colleagues,

00:55:10.494 --> 00:55:14.814
because I think that we
need to build a bigger tent.

00:55:14.814 --> 00:55:17.860
I will submit to you that
we are not going to win

00:55:17.860 --> 00:55:19.340
an election without political parties.

00:55:19.340 --> 00:55:22.237
And of course, my own civil
platform is a lynchpin of it.

00:55:22.237 --> 00:55:24.040
And is the most important, right?

00:55:24.040 --> 00:55:26.500
Because it is the most serious.

00:55:26.500 --> 00:55:30.740
It is the most experience
that has good people prepared

00:55:30.740 --> 00:55:31.790
to govern and so on.

00:55:31.790 --> 00:55:34.790
But a lot of people,
especially young people,

00:55:34.790 --> 00:55:36.760
dislike mainstream parties.

00:55:36.760 --> 00:55:38.530
So, we need to do something about it.

00:55:38.530 --> 00:55:40.336
Look at peace and look at the populist.

00:55:40.336 --> 00:55:44.800
As we say in Polish, they're
playing in different pianos

00:55:44.800 --> 00:55:46.400
at the same time, okay?

00:55:46.400 --> 00:55:49.470
So they strengthen the party,

00:55:49.470 --> 00:55:51.080
but they were building foundations,

00:55:51.080 --> 00:55:52.420
they were building discussion clubs.

00:55:52.420 --> 00:55:54.670
They were building internet platforms.

00:55:54.670 --> 00:55:56.210
They were doing grassroot movements.

00:55:56.210 --> 00:55:57.551
They were doing everything.

00:55:57.551 --> 00:56:00.810
And some of my colleagues say
platform, platform, platform.

00:56:00.810 --> 00:56:01.643
I love it.

00:56:01.643 --> 00:56:03.087
I say, we can chan
together, but I told them,

00:56:03.087 --> 00:56:05.470
no, we also need to add on.

00:56:05.470 --> 00:56:08.710
We need to consolidate the local mayors.

00:56:08.710 --> 00:56:09.543
And that's what we did.

00:56:09.543 --> 00:56:12.870
We have an association
movement that I've initiated

00:56:12.870 --> 00:56:13.870
of local mayors.

00:56:13.870 --> 00:56:15.400
Most of them are independent,

00:56:15.400 --> 00:56:17.600
but we stick together because if we don't,

00:56:17.600 --> 00:56:20.473
there will be either threatened
by peace or both by peace,

00:56:20.473 --> 00:56:22.760
or they will simply stop engaging

00:56:22.760 --> 00:56:24.700
in national politics, right?

00:56:24.700 --> 00:56:26.910
And this is again, coming
from my presidential campaign

00:56:26.910 --> 00:56:28.482
because in many places,

00:56:28.482 --> 00:56:31.910
I was there and the
local leader was with me.

00:56:31.910 --> 00:56:34.533
And that's why my result was so good.

00:56:35.420 --> 00:56:37.657
I'm gonna give you one example
from east and southern Poland

00:56:37.657 --> 00:56:39.750
and why I lost the election.

00:56:39.750 --> 00:56:44.341
First of all, there was
no even playing field,

00:56:44.341 --> 00:56:47.940
but one of the reasons is
that in our strongholds,

00:56:47.940 --> 00:56:52.550
we get 70%, and Peace
gets 30 in the big cities,

00:56:52.550 --> 00:56:54.640
in their strongholds, in
the eastern and rural areas.

00:56:54.640 --> 00:56:59.640
There are in Potaszniki, in
many counties, I got 10 or 15

00:57:01.069 --> 00:57:06.069
and Duda got, the president
of Poland, got 85% or 90%.

00:57:06.200 --> 00:57:08.880
There's one county in Powait Carpach,

00:57:09.759 --> 00:57:14.093
where there is a mayor who
used to be a cop in Warsaw.

00:57:15.500 --> 00:57:18.680
And he went and he said to the priest,

00:57:18.680 --> 00:57:22.440
I mean, if you keep on preaching
politics from the pulpit,

00:57:22.440 --> 00:57:25.370
you're not going to help
renovate the church.

00:57:25.370 --> 00:57:27.440
Stop it, okay?

00:57:27.440 --> 00:57:30.200
You keep on talking about Trzaskwski.

00:57:30.200 --> 00:57:33.029
It was because of Warsaw
that after the flood,

00:57:33.029 --> 00:57:35.810
Warsaw, as a sign of solidarity,

00:57:35.810 --> 00:57:38.931
they paved the roads and they help us out.

00:57:38.931 --> 00:57:43.931
And don't believe those lies

00:57:44.370 --> 00:57:46.610
about him trying to
change the way we live.

00:57:46.610 --> 00:57:48.660
I know him, he has a respect for tradition

00:57:48.660 --> 00:57:49.493
and so on and so forth.

00:57:49.493 --> 00:57:52.900
In this county, I got 35%, okay?

00:57:52.900 --> 00:57:56.003
Impossible to win, but 35 not 10 or 15.

00:57:56.003 --> 00:57:57.730
And when I go there, they tell me,

00:57:57.730 --> 00:57:59.410
I mean, if you come in your political hat,

00:57:59.410 --> 00:58:00.918
it's gonna be difficult.

00:58:00.918 --> 00:58:02.291
If you come as a mayor great, no problem.

00:58:02.291 --> 00:58:06.180
And thirdly, we've done a
campus Poland initiative

00:58:06.180 --> 00:58:08.870
where we invited thousand people,

00:58:08.870 --> 00:58:12.020
young people from all over
Poland, socially active.

00:58:12.020 --> 00:58:13.990
And for a week, we were
talking about the topics

00:58:13.990 --> 00:58:15.630
that they wanted to talk about.

00:58:15.630 --> 00:58:18.590
So, they wanted to talk
about women's rights,

00:58:18.590 --> 00:58:21.607
global warming, artificial
intelligence, and so on.

00:58:21.607 --> 00:58:23.900
And we were talking about,
I was there for a week.

00:58:23.900 --> 00:58:24.733
Many of them were afraid

00:58:24.733 --> 00:58:25.880
that we were going to indoctrinate them.

00:58:25.880 --> 00:58:27.076
No, it was an open debate.

00:58:27.076 --> 00:58:28.610
And many of my colleagues were there.

00:58:28.610 --> 00:58:30.510
We invited politicians,
we invited experts,

00:58:30.510 --> 00:58:31.990
we invited rock stars.

00:58:31.990 --> 00:58:32.900
We were having concerts.

00:58:32.900 --> 00:58:34.160
We were having sports activities

00:58:34.160 --> 00:58:37.167
and we've created an
alternative grassroot movement

00:58:37.167 --> 00:58:39.000
and a network which works.

00:58:39.000 --> 00:58:40.690
And now when I go to (indistinct)

00:58:40.690 --> 00:58:43.869
okay, of course, I'm
meeting with Platformer,

00:58:43.869 --> 00:58:45.390
but that's not enough.

00:58:45.390 --> 00:58:46.400
Because they're convinced people,

00:58:46.400 --> 00:58:47.640
but I'm meeting with the local leaders

00:58:47.640 --> 00:58:49.270
and I'm meeting with the young people,

00:58:49.270 --> 00:58:50.520
and they're local.

00:58:50.520 --> 00:58:51.542
So they tell me,

00:58:51.542 --> 00:58:54.510
those guys they will
vote for Peace forever.

00:58:54.510 --> 00:58:55.550
You can of course, talk to them,

00:58:55.550 --> 00:58:57.320
but be aware.

00:58:57.320 --> 00:58:58.270
These guys are yours.

00:58:58.270 --> 00:58:59.693
So say hi, but don't spend time

00:58:59.693 --> 00:59:01.334
because there are Platformer guys.

00:59:01.334 --> 00:59:04.192
Those are the guys you
need to be the convincing.

00:59:04.192 --> 00:59:08.400
So what I'm saying is that
I am absolutely convinced

00:59:08.400 --> 00:59:10.780
that the opposition parties,

00:59:10.780 --> 00:59:12.760
first of all, we all
have to be more mature

00:59:12.760 --> 00:59:17.210
and we have to collaborate
and start trusting each other.

00:59:17.210 --> 00:59:21.520
That's very important, but we
have to build a bigger tent

00:59:21.520 --> 00:59:24.053
and do what populists are doing,

00:59:24.053 --> 00:59:28.560
try to reach out and talk to the people

00:59:28.560 --> 00:59:29.790
who are not convinced.

00:59:29.790 --> 00:59:31.603
And by the way, the campus thing,

00:59:31.603 --> 00:59:35.510
80% of the people had
nothing to do with politics.

00:59:35.510 --> 00:59:37.440
There were political in a
sense that they were active,

00:59:37.440 --> 00:59:39.130
but they were not party political.

00:59:39.130 --> 00:59:41.543
Many of them, I hate my party.

00:59:42.500 --> 00:59:44.930
Some of them, not many, but some hate me,

00:59:44.930 --> 00:59:46.120
but they were there.

00:59:46.120 --> 00:59:47.379
And we had bounced ravage there.

00:59:47.379 --> 00:59:51.440
The founder of the shock therapy.

00:59:51.440 --> 00:59:53.390
For half of the young kids, he was a hero.

00:59:53.390 --> 00:59:54.223
He was God.

00:59:54.223 --> 00:59:56.226
For half of them, he was devil reincarnate

00:59:56.226 --> 00:59:58.369
because they were from the left.

00:59:58.369 --> 01:00:00.790
You should have seen the discussion.

01:00:00.790 --> 01:00:04.527
Whoa, I mean, how hard it was.

01:00:04.527 --> 01:00:06.147
And Andrezej was like this,

01:00:06.147 --> 01:00:08.939
because he's God at his university,

01:00:08.939 --> 01:00:10.660
it's not like he was
asked difficult questions.

01:00:10.660 --> 01:00:11.810
And guess what?

01:00:11.810 --> 01:00:14.150
They were pushing politicians
who were very cautious.

01:00:14.150 --> 01:00:18.340
Some of my friends to
be much more courageous

01:00:18.340 --> 01:00:20.785
because they were pushed so much.

01:00:20.785 --> 01:00:24.350
And the politicians are not
that used to having an open room

01:00:24.350 --> 01:00:26.730
and having hundreds of questions

01:00:26.730 --> 01:00:28.573
and then they need to answer them.

01:00:28.573 --> 01:00:30.683
So, I mean, that's my only answer.

01:00:30.683 --> 01:00:33.981
Talk to the unconvinced,
do the grass movement,

01:00:33.981 --> 01:00:35.440
be with the people.

01:00:35.440 --> 01:00:37.490
And that's a lesson from being a mayor,

01:00:37.490 --> 01:00:39.960
because you are just accountable.

01:00:39.960 --> 01:00:42.880
You walk the streets and all
the time you are ask questions.

01:00:42.880 --> 01:00:47.880
No other question, no other answer,

01:00:49.044 --> 01:00:50.094
but I remain hopeful.

01:00:52.903 --> 01:00:55.590
- Do we have time for another question?

01:00:55.590 --> 01:00:56.557
Okay, yes, please.

01:00:56.557 --> 01:01:00.910
- My name Desta, I applaud you
I'm as part of being Polish.

01:01:00.910 --> 01:01:03.390
I know Polish love refugees so much.

01:01:03.390 --> 01:01:06.490
My question for you as a mayor of Warsaw,

01:01:06.490 --> 01:01:11.490
I know that sometimes started
saying comes April 1st.

01:01:13.571 --> 01:01:17.810
They will stop helping the big expo places

01:01:17.810 --> 01:01:21.162
to have place for Ukraine refugees,

01:01:21.162 --> 01:01:25.450
and they decrease amount per day,

01:01:25.450 --> 01:01:27.970
how much they spend on immigrant refugee.

01:01:27.970 --> 01:01:29.770
I know that the good weather is coming.

01:01:29.770 --> 01:01:33.733
A lot of motels, hotels are
gonna need the tourist money.

01:01:33.733 --> 01:01:37.010
What is the immediate plan for Warsaw,

01:01:37.010 --> 01:01:39.170
you as a president and for other cities,

01:01:39.170 --> 01:01:40.640
according to help the refugees

01:01:40.640 --> 01:01:42.420
and relocate up somewhere else?

01:01:42.420 --> 01:01:44.640
- Great, two more questions and...

01:01:47.688 --> 01:01:48.521
- I'm Trakoswki,

01:01:48.521 --> 01:01:50.260
and Mr. Trzaskowski,

01:01:50.260 --> 01:01:53.990
I would like to know
from your perspective,

01:01:53.990 --> 01:01:57.580
how the whole crisis,

01:01:57.580 --> 01:02:00.713
I mean, coming back to your question also,

01:02:00.713 --> 01:02:05.713
how this crisis will actually
impact the budget of Warsaw

01:02:08.131 --> 01:02:09.876
and what is your plan?

01:02:09.876 --> 01:02:11.550
What are the counter measures

01:02:11.550 --> 01:02:13.558
that you would like to take,

01:02:13.558 --> 01:02:18.558
given the non-cooperative
government that we have?

01:02:18.750 --> 01:02:21.753
- Wonderful, both great questions, yeah.

01:02:23.673 --> 01:02:24.506
- Thank you for coming, Mayor.

01:02:25.447 --> 01:02:27.128
My name is Victor, I really
noticed in your lecture,

01:02:27.128 --> 01:02:29.686
the current government Polish government

01:02:29.686 --> 01:02:32.599
has experienced an incredible
turnaround in its public image

01:02:32.599 --> 01:02:34.810
and international standing
just the last two months.

01:02:34.810 --> 01:02:37.790
So from an outlier marked
by rule of law issues,

01:02:37.790 --> 01:02:40.240
abuse of gay and women rights,

01:02:40.240 --> 01:02:43.100
challenging international investors

01:02:43.100 --> 01:02:44.350
in their property rights,

01:02:45.299 --> 01:02:46.132
and a very damaging reaction

01:02:46.132 --> 01:02:48.530
to the U.S. presidential election, 2020,

01:02:48.530 --> 01:02:50.800
they became a strategic
partner of Brussels

01:02:50.800 --> 01:02:53.420
and Washington celebrated for a generous

01:02:53.420 --> 01:02:56.330
and courageous response
to concurrent prices.

01:02:56.330 --> 01:02:57.970
All that in just a months.

01:02:57.970 --> 01:03:00.580
My question is, do you
as one of the leaders

01:03:00.580 --> 01:03:03.160
of the opposition that has
been fighting those abuses

01:03:03.160 --> 01:03:04.423
for the last seven years,

01:03:04.423 --> 01:03:07.915
feel like the government is
getting passed from the west?

01:03:07.915 --> 01:03:09.865
It's been that of the hoop essentially.

01:03:09.865 --> 01:03:12.460
- My job is that they don't.

01:03:12.460 --> 01:03:17.460
Well, I mean, of course,
the most important thing

01:03:18.110 --> 01:03:19.000
is that we solve a problem,

01:03:19.000 --> 01:03:21.870
and I'm collaborating
with this government.

01:03:21.870 --> 01:03:24.130
And when it's below the radar,

01:03:24.130 --> 01:03:26.780
sometimes it's even a
good corporation, okay?

01:03:26.780 --> 01:03:29.160
But of course, they're pushing
most of the responsibility

01:03:29.160 --> 01:03:29.993
our way.

01:03:29.993 --> 01:03:31.400
And they promised the money

01:03:31.400 --> 01:03:32.844
and it's going to be
like with the pandemic.

01:03:32.844 --> 01:03:34.670
That at the beginning
we were collaborating

01:03:34.670 --> 01:03:37.370
and then they were pushing all
the responsibility our way.

01:03:37.370 --> 01:03:38.953
And they were taking money away from us.

01:03:38.953 --> 01:03:40.460
And one day were saying,

01:03:40.460 --> 01:03:42.350
I'm responsible for 11 hospitals.

01:03:42.350 --> 01:03:44.040
One hospital needs to be COVID.

01:03:44.040 --> 01:03:45.390
Okay, fine.

01:03:45.390 --> 01:03:46.810
And then they say, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no,

01:03:46.810 --> 01:03:50.320
all of your hospitals need
to have a COVID ward, okay?

01:03:50.320 --> 01:03:51.153
Okay.

01:03:51.153 --> 01:03:53.510
And then they suddenly set up a hospital

01:03:53.510 --> 01:03:54.760
at the national stadium

01:03:54.760 --> 01:03:56.950
and they pay all the
doctors three times more.

01:03:56.950 --> 01:03:58.830
So, all the doctors start working there

01:03:58.830 --> 01:03:59.960
and they don't have enough equipment.

01:03:59.960 --> 01:04:01.280
So when there's a serious case,

01:04:01.280 --> 01:04:02.986
all of those guys come to me, okay?

01:04:02.986 --> 01:04:05.280
That's a lack of strategy.

01:04:05.280 --> 01:04:07.110
And that's what I'm
afraid is going to happen

01:04:07.110 --> 01:04:08.120
this time around.

01:04:08.120 --> 01:04:10.683
So, I don't have my
own relocation strategy

01:04:10.683 --> 01:04:14.180
because we need a relocation strategy,

01:04:14.180 --> 01:04:16.770
not only on a national level,
but on a European level.

01:04:16.770 --> 01:04:17.603
Okay?

01:04:17.603 --> 01:04:18.730
And I am telling the government

01:04:18.730 --> 01:04:20.530
exactly what you've just told us.

01:04:20.530 --> 01:04:21.620
And I'm telling all of my friends

01:04:21.620 --> 01:04:23.310
in the European Union, in America,

01:04:23.310 --> 01:04:24.910
that this is going to end.

01:04:24.910 --> 01:04:26.170
We cannot do it indefinitely.

01:04:26.170 --> 01:04:28.290
That's why we need to
have a relocation scheme.

01:04:28.290 --> 01:04:32.248
That's why we might need
more reception centers,

01:04:32.248 --> 01:04:35.600
created by the UN agency
who know best how to do it.

01:04:35.600 --> 01:04:36.930
We don't have to invent a wheel.

01:04:36.930 --> 01:04:39.450
We have all of those guys on the ground,

01:04:39.450 --> 01:04:41.680
but they're just not authorized to work

01:04:41.680 --> 01:04:43.230
because there is no coordination.

01:04:43.230 --> 01:04:44.730
And there is no call for help.

01:04:44.730 --> 01:04:46.290
There's no memorandum understanding

01:04:46.290 --> 01:04:48.530
between the central government and them.

01:04:48.530 --> 01:04:50.697
And that's what we need because of course,

01:04:50.697 --> 01:04:54.124
we are retrofitting office spaces.

01:04:54.124 --> 01:04:57.030
I decided to keep those tents

01:04:57.030 --> 01:04:59.464
even though now we don't have
an influx of refugees open

01:04:59.464 --> 01:05:03.170
to prepare for a second
wave, but what can I do?

01:05:03.170 --> 01:05:05.940
I can prepare for 10,000
people, 15,000 people.

01:05:05.940 --> 01:05:07.987
I cannot prepare for another 100,000.

01:05:07.987 --> 01:05:10.060
And what if many people will simply say,

01:05:10.060 --> 01:05:13.270
okay, I cannot accept Ukrainians
any anymore at my home.

01:05:13.270 --> 01:05:14.810
Okay, now of course, there's a problem

01:05:14.810 --> 01:05:16.960
with those hotels that
you've mentioned and so on.

01:05:16.960 --> 01:05:18.450
That's why we need strategy.

01:05:18.450 --> 01:05:19.540
That's why we need help

01:05:19.540 --> 01:05:22.050
from the European Union financial help

01:05:22.050 --> 01:05:24.660
and relocation strategy, okay?

01:05:24.660 --> 01:05:27.690
Now, when it comes to the
government washing their hands,

01:05:27.690 --> 01:05:29.163
and I mean, first of all,

01:05:29.163 --> 01:05:32.780
we need to keep the pressure on those guys

01:05:32.780 --> 01:05:35.280
also for security reasons,

01:05:35.280 --> 01:05:38.030
because we need to be a strong democracy.

01:05:38.030 --> 01:05:39.190
And I know, and that's...

01:05:39.190 --> 01:05:41.760
I told that to President
Biden, when I had a chance,

01:05:41.760 --> 01:05:44.970
I told that to secretary
Blinken and they know it.

01:05:44.970 --> 01:05:47.060
I've told that on the hill,

01:05:47.060 --> 01:05:48.651
I'm telling that all my European friends,

01:05:48.651 --> 01:05:51.925
so that they need to remember that.

01:05:51.925 --> 01:05:54.300
And I also give them ready made recipes.

01:05:54.300 --> 01:05:57.610
I tell them, listen, if you
are connecting your money

01:05:57.610 --> 01:06:00.543
with rule of law, you put me
in a schizophrenic situation,

01:06:01.470 --> 01:06:05.110
because I cannot say that
I want the money to be...

01:06:05.110 --> 01:06:07.149
I don't want the money to be blocked.

01:06:07.149 --> 01:06:09.440
See, I'm so used to propaganda

01:06:09.440 --> 01:06:11.510
that I don't even say the sentence

01:06:11.510 --> 01:06:12.980
which can be cut out of context.

01:06:12.980 --> 01:06:17.100
So I don't want the money
to be blocked of course,

01:06:17.100 --> 01:06:22.100
and frozen, but they need to
be tough on the government.

01:06:22.390 --> 01:06:25.147
So I tell them, so give a
bit of money to us directly

01:06:25.147 --> 01:06:26.820
to the local governments.

01:06:26.820 --> 01:06:27.653
It's as easy as that.

01:06:27.653 --> 01:06:28.486
It's a win-win.

01:06:28.486 --> 01:06:29.853
Populist do not win cities.

01:06:30.700 --> 01:06:33.140
Make a huge program that
takes away diesel power buses

01:06:33.140 --> 01:06:34.680
from the streets of European cities

01:06:34.680 --> 01:06:38.050
and give them directly to the
cities which are ambitious.

01:06:38.050 --> 01:06:40.060
By the way, Warsaw was just announced

01:06:40.060 --> 01:06:42.910
one of the hundred green cities in Europe.

01:06:42.910 --> 01:06:44.920
We are in it, okay?

01:06:44.920 --> 01:06:46.860
Again, a bit of direct financing.

01:06:46.860 --> 01:06:49.690
That's what I was fighting
for for the past three years.

01:06:49.690 --> 01:06:51.420
So there are solutions

01:06:51.420 --> 01:06:54.250
and that's what I'm telling
our American friends.

01:06:54.250 --> 01:06:56.680
Most of them understand
it, but many of them,

01:06:56.680 --> 01:06:59.050
especially in Europe, would
want to use that as a pretext,

01:06:59.050 --> 01:07:04.050
because they are fed up with having to ask

01:07:04.670 --> 01:07:06.800
the peace government about it.

01:07:06.800 --> 01:07:11.370
But it's the job of ours, the
job of also public opinion

01:07:11.370 --> 01:07:14.020
to keep on pushing and to explain.

01:07:14.020 --> 01:07:16.070
And that's like to my American friends,

01:07:16.070 --> 01:07:16.903
that's what I'm saying.

01:07:16.903 --> 01:07:18.670
I'm not telling them all
values, values, values,

01:07:18.670 --> 01:07:22.260
because although Ukrainians
are actually dying

01:07:22.260 --> 01:07:23.453
for those values now.

01:07:25.050 --> 01:07:28.830
They're dying exactly for the
values that are undermined

01:07:28.830 --> 01:07:30.400
in some of our countries.

01:07:30.400 --> 01:07:34.260
But I tell them that
they need a strong ally.

01:07:34.260 --> 01:07:35.930
They need a credible ally.

01:07:35.930 --> 01:07:38.110
They need a democratic ally.

01:07:38.110 --> 01:07:39.080
They cannot afford...

01:07:39.080 --> 01:07:43.030
No one can afford Poland
to be now a weak democracy.

01:07:43.030 --> 01:07:45.550
So this is an incredibly important issue.

01:07:45.550 --> 01:07:47.979
And that's why this pressure
needs to be kept up.

01:07:47.979 --> 01:07:52.979
And that's why it is so
important and hopefully,

01:07:53.420 --> 01:07:55.320
I mean, this is not going to...

01:07:55.320 --> 01:07:57.209
And most of my colleagues,

01:07:57.209 --> 01:08:00.157
most of my interlocutors understand that.

01:08:00.157 --> 01:08:04.070
Honestly, there hasn't
been such a strong effect

01:08:04.070 --> 01:08:07.960
of rallying the flag as
some people expected.

01:08:07.960 --> 01:08:11.100
So that gives us hope that
at the end of the day,

01:08:11.100 --> 01:08:14.800
people polls, when it comes to elections,

01:08:14.800 --> 01:08:17.640
that they will take the
right decisions, okay?

01:08:17.640 --> 01:08:20.690
And that they will not forget
about what this government

01:08:20.690 --> 01:08:21.830
was doing.

01:08:21.830 --> 01:08:22.663
Okay?

01:08:22.663 --> 01:08:23.800
And it's also of course our job

01:08:23.800 --> 01:08:26.220
to make sure that happens.

01:08:26.220 --> 01:08:27.570
Okay?

01:08:27.570 --> 01:08:29.500
Did I omit any question?

01:08:29.500 --> 01:08:30.960
I think I've answered yours.

01:08:30.960 --> 01:08:31.793
Yes.

01:08:32.700 --> 01:08:36.250
Okay, I think I addressed
all the of questions.

01:08:36.250 --> 01:08:37.740
- Yeah.
- Yeah, guys.

01:08:37.740 --> 01:08:39.373
Yeah, I think, yes.

01:08:42.344 --> 01:08:43.177
- [Man] (indistinct).

01:08:43.177 --> 01:08:44.010
You know it's up to you.

01:08:44.010 --> 01:08:46.084
I mean, I can still answer lot.

01:08:46.084 --> 01:08:48.800
- [Listener] There actually two.

01:08:48.800 --> 01:08:52.260
So like one I will summarize
because people are like...

01:08:52.260 --> 01:08:53.669
- Sure. Shoot.

01:08:53.669 --> 01:08:56.140
- So for first question,

01:08:56.140 --> 01:09:01.140
regarding LGBTQIA plus
community rights in Poland

01:09:03.280 --> 01:09:08.280
and how you see their
future in Polish society,

01:09:08.620 --> 01:09:10.350
regarding current events

01:09:10.350 --> 01:09:13.320
and within the internal policy of Poland.

01:09:13.320 --> 01:09:17.030
And the second is more grounded

01:09:17.030 --> 01:09:19.588
to what's going on right now

01:09:19.588 --> 01:09:24.588
that the suggestion is
that many Polish people

01:09:25.440 --> 01:09:28.580
are going to be affected by
(indistinct) of the guests.

01:09:28.580 --> 01:09:33.268
And who that will be and what
will be the repercussions.

01:09:33.268 --> 01:09:36.179
- Oh, and last question.

01:09:36.179 --> 01:09:38.700
- (speaking in foreign language)

01:09:38.700 --> 01:09:42.109
Have a question that
maybe a broader question,

01:09:42.109 --> 01:09:45.330
back to the point that
you've been really stressing

01:09:45.330 --> 01:09:47.060
about the need for strategy.

01:09:47.060 --> 01:09:51.448
So, if we talk about European strategy

01:09:51.448 --> 01:09:52.690
in the wake of the war in Ukraine,

01:09:52.690 --> 01:09:54.555
or well, it's not really in the wake

01:09:54.555 --> 01:09:55.739
because the war's still going on,

01:09:55.739 --> 01:09:59.980
and I would love to get your thoughts

01:09:59.980 --> 01:10:04.200
about broader geopolitical
dimensions or strategy

01:10:04.200 --> 01:10:08.260
that is European Union's
policy or strategy

01:10:08.260 --> 01:10:10.700
on relations with Russia.

01:10:10.700 --> 01:10:14.980
What are key components of that strategy

01:10:14.980 --> 01:10:16.820
that you would like to see in place?

01:10:16.820 --> 01:10:17.653
That's one,

01:10:17.653 --> 01:10:19.770
and I'm asking that in addition

01:10:19.770 --> 01:10:23.620
to leading European countries,

01:10:23.620 --> 01:10:25.290
leading themselves of fossil fuels

01:10:25.290 --> 01:10:27.640
and especially Russian fossil fuels.

01:10:27.640 --> 01:10:31.730
So, what are some of the
other important components

01:10:31.730 --> 01:10:35.600
of such a European strategy?

01:10:35.600 --> 01:10:40.600
And I guess a second question
is who should be deciding it

01:10:40.740 --> 01:10:42.823
and how should this strategy be decided?

01:10:44.480 --> 01:10:46.140
Can you think of what according to you

01:10:46.140 --> 01:10:49.920
would be a good mechanism
of arriving at a viable

01:10:49.920 --> 01:10:52.836
and productive European strategy?

01:10:52.836 --> 01:10:56.880
Of course, ideally one that
is free from Hungarian,

01:10:56.880 --> 01:10:59.690
NITO and things like that nature.

01:10:59.690 --> 01:11:03.420
- Well, I mean, there is no
other place to make a strategy

01:11:03.420 --> 01:11:04.370
by the European council

01:11:04.370 --> 01:11:08.480
where all the heads of governments meet,

01:11:08.480 --> 01:11:10.220
and that's the place
to establish a strategy

01:11:10.220 --> 01:11:11.200
according to the treaties.

01:11:11.200 --> 01:11:13.630
And of course, there just
needs to be enough pressure

01:11:13.630 --> 01:11:18.630
on the Hungarians and all
the others not to water down.

01:11:18.820 --> 01:11:19.970
This is the most important thing.

01:11:19.970 --> 01:11:22.620
And of course, the important
thing is to keep up sanctions

01:11:22.620 --> 01:11:25.716
in place to strengthen Europe
when it comes to its defense

01:11:25.716 --> 01:11:27.843
and security dimension.

01:11:27.843 --> 01:11:31.700
To yes, to make Europe
independent of fossil fuels

01:11:31.700 --> 01:11:33.748
and speed up the transition.

01:11:33.748 --> 01:11:37.843
And also to do it in a way which is smart,

01:11:39.230 --> 01:11:43.870
to offer a serious perspective
to Ukrainian and to Moldova

01:11:43.870 --> 01:11:47.220
when it comes to the membership
of the European Union.

01:11:47.220 --> 01:11:52.190
At least those two countries,
but speed up the accession.

01:11:52.190 --> 01:11:55.900
And of course, to adopt a common policy

01:11:55.900 --> 01:11:58.930
when it comes to displaced people

01:11:58.930 --> 01:12:00.620
and have a relocation scheme,

01:12:00.620 --> 01:12:03.601
because this is immensely important.

01:12:03.601 --> 01:12:08.601
So, most of the elements
of the strategy are there,

01:12:10.340 --> 01:12:14.650
it's now just a question
to get them together

01:12:14.650 --> 01:12:15.540
and to put them together.

01:12:15.540 --> 01:12:20.053
And not to allow anyone to
water down as simple as that.

01:12:20.960 --> 01:12:22.902
or as difficult as that.

01:12:22.902 --> 01:12:23.735
And know...

01:12:23.735 --> 01:12:24.568
Yeah.

01:12:24.568 --> 01:12:25.850
- [Female] When you say stronger military,

01:12:25.850 --> 01:12:27.620
do you mean within the structures of NATO

01:12:27.620 --> 01:12:28.530
or outside of the structure?

01:12:28.530 --> 01:12:30.940
- Both, I mean, we have
the structures ready

01:12:30.940 --> 01:12:32.960
because we do not want to duplicate NATO.

01:12:32.960 --> 01:12:36.050
And after the Warsaw summit,
we know how to strengthen NATO,

01:12:36.050 --> 01:12:37.925
but also strengthen
the European dimension,

01:12:37.925 --> 01:12:41.230
which is part of the same
system as if a second leg.

01:12:41.230 --> 01:12:43.740
There is no talk about the competition,

01:12:43.740 --> 01:12:46.530
but for example, all the
things that now we are doing,

01:12:46.530 --> 01:12:48.640
like providing lethal weapons,

01:12:48.640 --> 01:12:51.990
I mean, it was unthinkable
a few months ago

01:12:51.990 --> 01:12:52.850
that you could do it.

01:12:52.850 --> 01:12:55.413
Now, it's just a question
of better coordinating it.

01:12:56.290 --> 01:12:58.320
And of course, part of that strategy

01:12:58.320 --> 01:13:00.470
also is not only a
European Union strategy,

01:13:00.470 --> 01:13:01.330
but NATO strategy.

01:13:01.330 --> 01:13:05.125
For example, we do not do rotating basis,

01:13:05.125 --> 01:13:09.320
but permanent NATO basis
in Poland or in Romania

01:13:09.320 --> 01:13:10.830
or in the Baltic States,

01:13:10.830 --> 01:13:13.700
because of course, there is
also security dimension to it.

01:13:13.700 --> 01:13:17.690
Now when it comes to
gas and we are for now,

01:13:17.690 --> 01:13:22.380
we are prepared also because
of most of the things

01:13:22.380 --> 01:13:24.550
that we've done under the energy union,

01:13:24.550 --> 01:13:27.840
but of course, that needs
the reliance of the system

01:13:27.840 --> 01:13:31.240
and of our allies, which
needs providing us with gas.

01:13:31.240 --> 01:13:32.289
And of course,

01:13:32.289 --> 01:13:36.610
we need to prepare for
the more difficult months

01:13:36.610 --> 01:13:38.170
and we need European solidarity.

01:13:38.170 --> 01:13:40.770
It was announced, but now we
need to put it in practice.

01:13:40.770 --> 01:13:42.760
And also the international solidarity,

01:13:42.760 --> 01:13:46.710
we are finishing the connections
with the Norwegian fields,

01:13:46.710 --> 01:13:48.774
but of course, we can
import gas from the U.S.

01:13:48.774 --> 01:13:49.607
and so on and so forth.

01:13:49.607 --> 01:13:51.880
I think that President
Biden just yesterday,

01:13:51.880 --> 01:13:53.240
indicated referenced it.

01:13:53.240 --> 01:13:55.850
So, let's hope that we'll
go into that direction.

01:13:55.850 --> 01:13:58.570
And again at the end of the day,

01:13:58.570 --> 01:14:01.550
it is peace governing in Poland.

01:14:01.550 --> 01:14:04.890
And of course, we have
inflation everywhere,

01:14:04.890 --> 01:14:07.270
but more so in Poland.

01:14:07.270 --> 01:14:10.100
And this is because of
some crazy decisions

01:14:10.100 --> 01:14:11.500
of the central bank,

01:14:11.500 --> 01:14:16.210
which is in the hands of the peace crony.

01:14:16.210 --> 01:14:19.400
And of course, we need to
also explain to the people

01:14:19.400 --> 01:14:23.780
that most of the all of the
decisions were taken by peace

01:14:23.780 --> 01:14:28.675
and that they need to be held accountable

01:14:28.675 --> 01:14:33.426
at the elections that are coming.

01:14:33.426 --> 01:14:38.350
And the last but not
least, the LGBTQ community.

01:14:38.350 --> 01:14:42.821
I mean, these guys, the
peace guys, the government,

01:14:42.821 --> 01:14:43.654
the Polish government was trying,

01:14:43.654 --> 01:14:45.730
they always need to have an enemy.

01:14:45.730 --> 01:14:47.150
And I think that they've used

01:14:47.150 --> 01:14:48.540
because of my presidential campaign,

01:14:48.540 --> 01:14:50.883
they've used all kinds
of arguments they could

01:14:50.883 --> 01:14:53.870
in order to attack me, to
attack the LGBT community.

01:14:53.870 --> 01:14:56.380
And I think that they went so far

01:14:56.380 --> 01:14:57.697
that they've just ridiculed themselves.

01:14:57.697 --> 01:15:00.450
I'm just gonna give you one example,

01:15:00.450 --> 01:15:03.928
because not all of you have
followed the Polish politics,

01:15:03.928 --> 01:15:07.513
I've signed the LGBT
charter as the first mayor

01:15:07.513 --> 01:15:10.310
and I'm now the only mayor
in Poland to help out

01:15:10.310 --> 01:15:11.430
the LGBT community.

01:15:11.430 --> 01:15:13.750
And we've said that in this document,

01:15:13.750 --> 01:15:17.370
it says that we are going
to use the WHO standards,

01:15:17.370 --> 01:15:20.400
World Health Organization as a benchmark.

01:15:20.400 --> 01:15:22.680
What the Peace propaganda did,

01:15:22.680 --> 01:15:25.750
they took a booklet from WHO

01:15:25.750 --> 01:15:27.640
written by experts for teachers,

01:15:27.640 --> 01:15:30.470
explaining how children develop,

01:15:30.470 --> 01:15:32.700
that they get interested in
their bodies with their age

01:15:32.700 --> 01:15:35.330
and then they start masturbating
when they're 12 and so on.

01:15:35.330 --> 01:15:38.070
And for three weeks, they've
unleashed this campaign

01:15:38.070 --> 01:15:41.893
that I want to teach masturbation
to children at school.

01:15:43.740 --> 01:15:46.460
And that was like the key
argument that they had

01:15:46.460 --> 01:15:48.050
throughout the campaign.

01:15:48.050 --> 01:15:49.990
And of course, everyone
in Warsaw and Poland

01:15:49.990 --> 01:15:51.522
cracker was laughing
like you are laughing,

01:15:51.522 --> 01:15:53.872
but in the rural areas,
they were not laughing,

01:15:55.110 --> 01:15:57.669
but they've went so far

01:15:57.669 --> 01:15:59.667
that now when I go and
travel around Poland

01:15:59.667 --> 01:16:04.460
and I talk to people, they
know that it's just not true.

01:16:04.460 --> 01:16:05.810
Okay?

01:16:05.810 --> 01:16:09.130
So of course, we will keep on
defending all the minorities.

01:16:09.130 --> 01:16:11.124
And by the way, I'm not a crazy leftist

01:16:11.124 --> 01:16:12.860
as they try to portray me.

01:16:12.860 --> 01:16:15.890
I'm just this my job as a mayor.

01:16:15.890 --> 01:16:20.750
If someone gets by and is
successful, my job is not to medal

01:16:22.410 --> 01:16:23.400
because they get by.

01:16:23.400 --> 01:16:25.420
And if I have people who have problems

01:16:25.420 --> 01:16:27.700
or they're marginalized or attacked,

01:16:27.700 --> 01:16:29.760
my job is to help them
because I'm a mayor.

01:16:29.760 --> 01:16:32.057
And it doesn't matter whether
they're senior citizens,

01:16:32.057 --> 01:16:36.820
people with disabilities, LGBT minorities,

01:16:36.820 --> 01:16:39.330
all kinds of minorities,
we are there to help.

01:16:39.330 --> 01:16:42.074
And that's a normal standard
of a democratic country.

01:16:42.074 --> 01:16:45.400
And I think that we were
driving that point home

01:16:45.400 --> 01:16:46.730
all the time.

01:16:46.730 --> 01:16:48.970
And I hope that we are in a
different place when it comes...

01:16:48.970 --> 01:16:50.640
I mean, it will be very difficult,

01:16:50.640 --> 01:16:52.560
again, to unleash this campaign.

01:16:52.560 --> 01:16:54.400
People have heard all the arguments,

01:16:54.400 --> 01:16:58.063
and they look around and nothing changed.

01:16:59.440 --> 01:17:03.782
I still have two kids, same
wife and a dog and a parrot,

01:17:03.782 --> 01:17:05.430
(participant laughs)

01:17:05.430 --> 01:17:07.960
and our way of life is not threatened

01:17:07.960 --> 01:17:09.690
because we've signed an LGBT Charter.

01:17:09.690 --> 01:17:13.630
And we say that we should be
protecting everyone's rights

01:17:13.630 --> 01:17:16.493
and that's the foundations
of the democratic society.

01:17:17.600 --> 01:17:18.830
So, I think that...

01:17:18.830 --> 01:17:21.980
And many people say that I lost
the election because of that

01:17:21.980 --> 01:17:23.210
and so on and so forth.

01:17:23.210 --> 01:17:26.020
But at least, people saw
that there are politicians

01:17:26.020 --> 01:17:28.949
in Poland who do things
that they believe in.

01:17:28.949 --> 01:17:32.520
And that's worthwhile in itself.

01:17:32.520 --> 01:17:36.820
And we've opened doors to
start discussing subjects

01:17:36.820 --> 01:17:38.232
that maybe were taboo for a while.

01:17:38.232 --> 01:17:40.963
By the way, not easy anywhere.

01:17:41.990 --> 01:17:45.880
When was the judgment of the Supreme Court

01:17:45.880 --> 01:17:49.130
of the United States
on same sex marriages?

01:17:49.130 --> 01:17:50.570
2015?

01:17:50.570 --> 01:17:54.130
It wasn't 50 years ago,
and don't get me started.

01:17:54.130 --> 01:17:54.963
Okay.

01:17:56.121 --> 01:17:59.111
So, I mean, it's not that
we have our variants,

01:17:59.111 --> 01:18:00.330
or we don't understand
that sometimes we hear.

01:18:00.330 --> 01:18:02.010
We just need people with guts

01:18:02.010 --> 01:18:03.600
to start debating these things

01:18:04.910 --> 01:18:09.900
and explaining to people that
this is what we should do.

01:18:09.900 --> 01:18:11.960
This is the right thing to do.

01:18:11.960 --> 01:18:15.750
And on top of that, explaining
that there is no ideology,

01:18:15.750 --> 01:18:18.160
there are just people and no ideology,

01:18:18.160 --> 01:18:20.820
and that no one threatens our way of life.

01:18:20.820 --> 01:18:22.220
Look at the European Union.

01:18:22.220 --> 01:18:27.030
I mean, we collaborate, we
build a community together

01:18:27.030 --> 01:18:29.580
and it strengthens our national identity.

01:18:29.580 --> 01:18:30.480
Doesn't weaken it.

01:18:31.520 --> 01:18:33.630
And it strengths not
only the French identity,

01:18:33.630 --> 01:18:36.983
but also the identity and Pole identity,

01:18:36.983 --> 01:18:40.980
also Kasian identity in Poland.

01:18:40.980 --> 01:18:43.070
That's what we should be doing.

01:18:43.070 --> 01:18:46.820
And do you see, I don't
know, Italians from Florence,

01:18:46.820 --> 01:18:47.900
like fretting about it,

01:18:47.900 --> 01:18:49.910
or I'm gonna lose my Florence identity.

01:18:49.910 --> 01:18:51.900
I will start speaking, I don't know,

01:18:51.900 --> 01:18:54.930
with a Roman accent because
of the European Union.

01:18:54.930 --> 01:18:57.449
No, okay?

01:18:57.449 --> 01:19:00.490
I'm not losing my Polish identity.

01:19:00.490 --> 01:19:02.980
I'm not losing my Warsaw identity

01:19:02.980 --> 01:19:04.890
because I'm also European.

01:19:04.890 --> 01:19:07.410
And we need to drive
that point home, okay?

01:19:07.410 --> 01:19:09.630
And I think that either you have guts

01:19:09.630 --> 01:19:11.870
to start these debates, or you don't,

01:19:11.870 --> 01:19:16.216
but I hope that we've started
these debates in Poland.

01:19:16.216 --> 01:19:19.670
And now we just need to hold
this government accountable.

01:19:19.670 --> 01:19:20.570
Okay?

01:19:20.570 --> 01:19:23.429
And here I'm finishing, we
need to keep the pressure up.

01:19:23.429 --> 01:19:24.430
Okay?

01:19:24.430 --> 01:19:29.430
Because if I see that
in a Ukrainian crisis,

01:19:29.550 --> 01:19:32.100
one of the NGOs, which
got the biggest support

01:19:32.100 --> 01:19:35.010
from the national government
in Poland is Mr. Bulgeich,

01:19:35.010 --> 01:19:37.680
a crazy fascist guy who's organizing

01:19:37.680 --> 01:19:40.630
those marches around Warsaw,

01:19:40.630 --> 01:19:42.773
which George of my city and these guys

01:19:42.773 --> 01:19:45.510
are sometimes pronouncing words

01:19:45.510 --> 01:19:47.457
which are simply racist and so on.

01:19:47.457 --> 01:19:49.770
And they got support
because they've accepted

01:19:49.770 --> 01:19:51.120
some Ukrainians.

01:19:51.120 --> 01:19:53.860
And they've millions from the government,

01:19:53.860 --> 01:19:54.700
millions of support.

01:19:54.700 --> 01:19:57.420
And then I talked to an NGO, LA Strada,

01:19:57.420 --> 01:19:59.120
who is fighting with women trafficking

01:19:59.120 --> 01:20:00.370
and with forced prostitution.

01:20:00.370 --> 01:20:02.400
And they tell me finally, we can work.

01:20:02.400 --> 01:20:03.530
And I said, "What happened?"

01:20:03.530 --> 01:20:04.790
And I said, "You support us,

01:20:04.790 --> 01:20:06.960
but we got this additional grant

01:20:06.960 --> 01:20:10.970
from American donors,
$5,000, and we can work."

01:20:10.970 --> 01:20:11.803
Okay?

01:20:12.730 --> 01:20:14.020
And here I'm driving point home.

01:20:14.020 --> 01:20:16.137
I mean, please go and spread the message.

01:20:16.137 --> 01:20:20.340
NGOs in Poland need support, okay?

01:20:20.340 --> 01:20:21.670
Local government needs support,

01:20:21.670 --> 01:20:23.150
volunteers need support.

01:20:23.150 --> 01:20:25.220
And even if the credit goes

01:20:25.220 --> 01:20:27.340
and then suddenly everyone
loves the United States,

01:20:27.340 --> 01:20:30.870
fine, let them love him, but help us.

01:20:30.870 --> 01:20:33.650
Because at the end of the
day, what you see in Poland,

01:20:33.650 --> 01:20:35.200
it's not a miracle.

01:20:35.200 --> 01:20:38.820
It's just solidarity and
it is the civil society.

01:20:38.820 --> 01:20:40.180
It is the non-government organization.

01:20:40.180 --> 01:20:42.910
It's the charities who do that.

01:20:42.910 --> 01:20:44.150
And that's why we need to help them.

01:20:44.150 --> 01:20:46.840
And that's why I'm not in a junket,

01:20:46.840 --> 01:20:50.800
but I'm trying to convince
the American public opinion,

01:20:50.800 --> 01:20:55.090
the donors, the NGOs,
the political foundations

01:20:55.090 --> 01:20:56.170
and so on,

01:20:56.170 --> 01:20:58.814
that we all need to get our act together

01:20:58.814 --> 01:21:01.250
and that we should not lose focus

01:21:01.250 --> 01:21:03.300
from the state of democracy in Poland,

01:21:03.300 --> 01:21:06.480
because Poland needs to be in
lynchpin of European security.

01:21:06.480 --> 01:21:08.930
And at the end again and again and again,

01:21:08.930 --> 01:21:11.010
Ukrainians are fighting
for our freedom too,

01:21:11.010 --> 01:21:12.383
for yours too, guys.

01:21:13.270 --> 01:21:16.689
And for the stability of
Trans-Atlantic Alliance,

01:21:16.689 --> 01:21:18.780
and for the values that we are preaching

01:21:18.780 --> 01:21:20.720
and we talking about, and
they're dying for them.

01:21:20.720 --> 01:21:21.790
And at the end of the day,

01:21:21.790 --> 01:21:25.647
remember that all the bad
guys in the world are looking.

01:21:25.647 --> 01:21:30.647
So, we need to prove to them
that we are going to be tough

01:21:31.190 --> 01:21:33.690
and united and we are
going to draw the lessons

01:21:33.690 --> 01:21:36.950
and it's not worthwhile to start wars,

01:21:36.950 --> 01:21:40.030
attack sovereign nations,
attack people, kill them,

01:21:40.030 --> 01:21:41.980
rape them, because otherwise,

01:21:41.980 --> 01:21:43.570
we are going to end up in a situation

01:21:43.570 --> 01:21:46.330
like we end up in Warsaw
and of course, in Ukraine.

01:21:46.330 --> 01:21:47.490
Okay?

01:21:47.490 --> 01:21:48.830
So, that's why we should
be spreading the message.

01:21:48.830 --> 01:21:50.900
And if you tell me, will the world forget?

01:21:50.900 --> 01:21:53.560
Maybe, but it's our job guys, yours too.

01:21:53.560 --> 01:21:56.330
Some of you are Polish, Lavtian,
some of you are Ukrainian,

01:21:56.330 --> 01:21:57.630
but many of you are American.

01:21:57.630 --> 01:21:59.393
Just go out and spread the message.

01:22:00.280 --> 01:22:02.414
And come to Warsaw, it's not a war zone,

01:22:02.414 --> 01:22:06.323
help us out, leave a lot of money.

01:22:06.323 --> 01:22:08.450
(audience laughs)

01:22:08.450 --> 01:22:09.634
Thank you.

01:22:09.634 --> 01:22:12.634
(audience clapping)

01:22:19.298 --> 01:22:21.798
(soft music)

